1
00:01:08,741 --> 00:01:10,621
I've got orders from the mill.

2
00:01:10,981 --> 00:01:13,101
To my luck, I have no people
to help cut down the sugarcanes.

3
00:01:13,261 --> 00:01:15,221
If you know anyone,
please send them my way.

4
00:01:15,381 --> 00:01:16,821
Sure, I'll see to it.

5
00:01:18,501 --> 00:01:20,701
[phone rings]

6
00:01:32,541 --> 00:01:34,141
[phone rings]

7
00:01:42,821 --> 00:01:44,701
[phone rings]

8
00:01:49,941 --> 00:01:51,820
- Hello, sir?
- [in Malayalam] You called, Selvi?

9
00:01:51,821 --> 00:01:54,021
Yes, sir. I'll work for you.

10
00:01:54,181 --> 00:01:55,181
- Over here?
- Yes, sir.

11
00:01:55,341 --> 00:01:58,300
- Hop on the Tuesday train, then.
- No, I'm coming right away.

12
00:01:58,301 --> 00:01:59,581
I'll hang up, sir.

13
00:02:05,301 --> 00:02:06,661
[phone rings]

14
00:02:13,981 --> 00:02:15,461
[phone rings]

15
00:02:23,061 --> 00:02:24,941
[phone rings]

16
00:02:32,941 --> 00:02:34,141
Who's going at this hour?

17
00:02:35,301 --> 00:02:36,381
Answer me!

18
00:02:37,621 --> 00:02:39,301
Brother Mani, it's me!

19
00:02:39,421 --> 00:02:40,701
- Selvi.
- Ah, Selvi!

20
00:02:40,821 --> 00:02:43,461
- What are you doing all alone?
- I…

21
00:02:43,701 --> 00:02:45,861
We're on a pilgrimage walk
to Melmaruvathur.

22
00:02:46,021 --> 00:02:49,341
- They're waiting for me at Kalarikuppam.
- Stay safe, then.

23
00:02:49,461 --> 00:02:51,141
Watch your step.

24
00:02:52,261 --> 00:02:53,581
Ah, a bus…

25
00:02:53,701 --> 00:02:56,301
Wait! Stop!

26
00:02:56,461 --> 00:02:58,061
Stop! Please!

27
00:02:58,501 --> 00:02:59,901
Stop for me, please!

28
00:03:00,101 --> 00:03:01,901
Please!

29
00:03:14,901 --> 00:03:17,901
Oh, look!
What an eye candy at this hour?!

30
00:03:18,061 --> 00:03:20,181
Careful, this must be
a honey-trap like situation.

31
00:03:20,341 --> 00:03:22,180
- Don't stop. Keep moving.
- Hello!

32
00:03:22,181 --> 00:03:23,501
Please stop!

33
00:03:30,221 --> 00:03:32,781
[group singing a devotional song]

34
00:04:23,021 --> 00:04:25,661
Lord Ayyanar, save me!

35
00:04:46,461 --> 00:04:52,101
NOORU SAMI

36
00:05:06,741 --> 00:05:09,741
I’ve got to start work
from tomorrow, Uncle.

37
00:05:10,261 --> 00:05:14,220
Now that their dad's no more,

38
00:05:14,221 --> 00:05:16,781
they'll now have to endure
my torture.

39
00:05:16,941 --> 00:05:20,381
If you could be with the children
till they grow up,

40
00:05:20,781 --> 00:05:23,141
I can take good care of you all.

41
00:05:24,541 --> 00:05:27,901
We don’t want to depend on you
more than we already do.

42
00:05:28,461 --> 00:05:31,101
Why don't you ask your parents?

43
00:05:31,901 --> 00:05:34,540
The well at Melakadu dried up, Selvi.

44
00:05:34,541 --> 00:05:37,140
I must get it up and running
to water the fields.

45
00:05:37,141 --> 00:05:39,661
I can't abandon it all now,
just to be with you, dear.

46
00:05:39,901 --> 00:05:42,581
- The saltfish's for you!
- Selvi,

47
00:05:43,381 --> 00:05:45,421
I can't look after it
all by myself.

48
00:05:45,941 --> 00:05:47,061
Let Dad be with me.

49
00:05:47,221 --> 00:05:48,541
Take Mom with you.

50
00:05:50,381 --> 00:05:51,861
Here, have some more curry.

51
00:05:52,101 --> 00:05:52,981
Enough for me.

52
00:05:53,101 --> 00:05:54,061
Selvi…

53
00:05:55,461 --> 00:05:57,540
Why don't you build a makeshift
place near us?

54
00:05:57,541 --> 00:05:59,141
- Granny, feed me!
- Eat, dear.

55
00:06:00,261 --> 00:06:03,461
Like Dad's bothered about his fields,
and you leaving him,

56
00:06:03,661 --> 00:06:06,741
I'm worried about my kids
and their education.

57
00:06:07,101 --> 00:06:09,020
- Hey…
- Come along, boys!

58
00:06:09,021 --> 00:06:11,380
- Selvi, wait!
- Hear me out, my child.

59
00:06:11,381 --> 00:06:13,341
- Don't go.
- Bye-bye, all of you!

60
00:06:13,501 --> 00:06:17,021
- Come.
- Such a stubborn girl I have!

61
00:06:20,341 --> 00:06:21,541
Here you go.

62
00:06:23,221 --> 00:06:26,421
Your children's future is now
a priority, Selvi.

63
00:06:26,821 --> 00:06:28,620
If they join us this year,

64
00:06:28,621 --> 00:06:31,461
they can study for free
until they graduate.

65
00:06:38,221 --> 00:06:41,421
- Go on. Eat up, you two.
- Why can't we study here?

66
00:06:43,701 --> 00:06:46,500
- How dare you to toss your plate away!
- Mom, please!

67
00:06:46,501 --> 00:06:49,141
- Don't you ever do that!
- Mom, I'm sorry! Please don't hit me!

68
00:06:49,421 --> 00:06:52,141
It's for your own good!
That's final.

69
00:06:52,301 --> 00:06:53,981
You are going. Is that clear?

70
00:06:54,141 --> 00:06:56,621
Clear?
You're going with him, too.

71
00:07:06,301 --> 00:07:08,500
Selvi?
Selvi, please don't!

72
00:07:08,501 --> 00:07:10,780
Don't make a fuss now, Vivek.

73
00:07:10,781 --> 00:07:12,381
Let… let go of my hands!

74
00:07:12,541 --> 00:07:13,780
Grab his suitcase, Baskar!

75
00:07:13,781 --> 00:07:15,421
- Please, don't send us!
- Vivek!

76
00:07:15,581 --> 00:07:19,301
Throw all the tantrums you want!
You’re still going.

77
00:07:19,421 --> 00:07:20,741
Catch hold of him, Baskar.

78
00:07:21,501 --> 00:07:23,261
Do you want to get it good
like yesterday?

79
00:07:23,461 --> 00:07:25,980
Don't make me hit you too, Baskar.

80
00:07:25,981 --> 00:07:27,821
- Ma'am, can you hold him down?
- I'll take care of him.

81
00:07:27,981 --> 00:07:30,981
You'll be fine. Trust me.
Why are you at my feet?

82
00:07:31,141 --> 00:07:33,741
See, there are many kids
like you inside.

83
00:07:33,941 --> 00:07:37,221
Listen, you'll be fine.
Stop crying for nothing!

84
00:07:37,381 --> 00:07:39,461
Stop whining and get in, Baskar!

85
00:07:40,221 --> 00:07:43,861
[both] Mom! Mom!
Please don't send us away!

86
00:07:44,141 --> 00:07:48,821
Please!
Let us stay here and study!

87
00:07:48,941 --> 00:07:52,581
See?
Kids your age are so quiet.

88
00:07:52,741 --> 00:07:56,060
You'll make many friends!
Please stop crying.

89
00:07:56,061 --> 00:07:59,340
- Mom! Mom, please!
- Take us with you, please!

90
00:07:59,341 --> 00:08:00,980
Let us stay with you, Mom!

91
00:08:00,981 --> 00:08:03,461
Don't send us away, Mom! Please!

92
00:08:03,941 --> 00:08:06,980
- Mom, they're starting the bus!
- Please, please, take us with you!

93
00:08:06,981 --> 00:08:08,860
[both] Mom! Mom! Mom!

94
00:08:08,861 --> 00:08:13,701
- Don't go away, please!
- Mom! Mom!

95
00:08:48,341 --> 00:08:50,340
My babies!

96
00:08:50,341 --> 00:08:55,661
♪ Even if all the gods appear
Even if they stand so near ♪

97
00:08:55,781 --> 00:08:58,621
♪ Mother stands above them all ♪

98
00:09:01,221 --> 00:09:06,660
♪ Even if sky and earth unite
Even if they fill our sight ♪

99
00:09:06,661 --> 00:09:09,541
♪ Mother stands above them all ♪

100
00:09:12,301 --> 00:09:17,301
♪ Sometimes a flame
Sometimes a calm shade ♪

101
00:09:17,501 --> 00:09:20,701
♪ She shifts for your sake ♪

102
00:09:23,181 --> 00:09:28,181
♪ Even in struggle
Even in hunger ♪

103
00:09:28,341 --> 00:09:30,981
♪ She gives all she has ♪

104
00:09:34,101 --> 00:09:39,140
♪ When the world stands in our way
When even our own say no ♪

105
00:09:39,141 --> 00:09:44,021
♪ She stands with us still ♪

106
00:09:45,021 --> 00:09:50,060
♪ She becomes the burning wick
Her dreams become the fire ♪

107
00:09:50,061 --> 00:09:54,381
♪ She shines as our guiding light ♪

108
00:09:54,861 --> 00:09:57,341
♪ Mother’s love… ♪

109
00:09:57,501 --> 00:10:00,581
♪ A love so pure ♪

110
00:10:00,821 --> 00:10:06,061
♪ No need for words to say
Love is felt in every way ♪

111
00:10:06,221 --> 00:10:11,261
♪ Mother holds it all inside
My eyes won’t ever hide ♪

112
00:10:11,501 --> 00:10:17,060
♪ No need for words to say
Love is felt in every way ♪

113
00:10:17,061 --> 00:10:22,301
♪ Mother holds it all inside
My eyes won’t ever hide ♪

114
00:10:32,941 --> 00:10:34,821
Look at this!
That's Oman's currency.

115
00:10:35,341 --> 00:10:36,620
Bas, it's Singapore's.

116
00:10:36,621 --> 00:10:38,661
- Hush now and study.
- Look at Australia's!

117
00:10:38,781 --> 00:10:40,821
- Sir, your passport.
- Please be on time for your flight.

118
00:10:42,141 --> 00:10:43,061
Brother…

119
00:10:44,061 --> 00:10:45,421
Give it to Sir.
I'll take it from him.

120
00:10:46,221 --> 00:10:47,861
Please take it from her, sir.

121
00:10:48,981 --> 00:10:50,300
- Here you go.
- Thank you!

122
00:10:50,301 --> 00:10:51,381
See you.

123
00:10:51,701 --> 00:10:54,581
Don’t take this the wrong way,
but from tomorrow,

124
00:10:55,261 --> 00:10:56,861
please wear a bindi
when you come in.

125
00:10:59,981 --> 00:11:05,461
♪ At first sight,
Her eyes would cry ♪

126
00:11:05,581 --> 00:11:10,621
♪ At my first words,
Her face lit joy ♪

127
00:11:10,941 --> 00:11:16,021
♪ When I slip,
She sets me straight ♪

128
00:11:16,381 --> 00:11:21,581
♪ She fixes my flaws
Makes me great ♪

129
00:11:21,781 --> 00:11:26,621
♪ For our dreams to rise… ♪

130
00:11:32,221 --> 00:11:37,421
♪ For our dreams to rise
She waits with hopeful eyes ♪

131
00:11:37,581 --> 00:11:42,461
♪ Who like a mother walks this earth? ♪

132
00:11:43,501 --> 00:11:48,261
♪ She bears pain we'll never know ♪

133
00:11:48,461 --> 00:11:52,101
♪ She’s the root from which we grow ♪

134
00:11:52,821 --> 00:11:54,621
It's for my kids' education.

135
00:11:54,741 --> 00:11:56,061
I can't lend you that much.

136
00:11:56,301 --> 00:11:57,700
- Please leave!
- Sir, please!

137
00:11:57,701 --> 00:11:59,621
I can't decide this alone. I'll discuss
with the other three partners.

138
00:11:59,821 --> 00:12:04,061
♪…all inside
My eyes won’t ever hide ♪

139
00:12:04,261 --> 00:12:09,621
♪ No need for words to say
Love is felt in every way ♪

140
00:12:09,781 --> 00:12:14,821
♪ Mother holds it all inside
My eyes won’t ever hide ♪

141
00:12:40,061 --> 00:12:44,341
I endured through things
I can’t bring myself to tell my kids,

142
00:12:45,221 --> 00:12:48,381
because they were with me.

143
00:12:48,821 --> 00:12:50,021
[door knocks]

144
00:12:50,701 --> 00:12:53,421
Selvi? Selvi!

145
00:12:54,061 --> 00:12:55,421
Slept already?

146
00:12:55,741 --> 00:12:57,781
Can you come to the backyard?

147
00:12:58,061 --> 00:13:01,661
I'll write you up an acre in return!

148
00:13:03,261 --> 00:13:05,741
Selvi? Hey, Sel!

149
00:13:06,221 --> 00:13:08,061
Give me your number.

150
00:13:08,541 --> 00:13:11,861
I've written mine on your window.

151
00:13:12,381 --> 00:13:14,381
Call me when you can.

152
00:13:16,261 --> 00:13:17,341
Selvi?

153
00:13:17,501 --> 00:13:20,581
I heard you asked the financier for money
for your sons' education.

154
00:13:20,741 --> 00:13:23,301
You could've come to me, first!

155
00:13:23,581 --> 00:13:25,901
We're all going to die anyway.

156
00:13:26,021 --> 00:13:27,661
So, let's live the night to the fullest!

157
00:13:31,381 --> 00:13:33,180
Is there any place in this world

158
00:13:33,181 --> 00:13:36,020
where a woman living alone

159
00:13:36,021 --> 00:13:38,181
is treated with dignity and respect?

160
00:13:50,541 --> 00:13:51,981
PUBERTY CEREMONY
C. VANATHI (A) CHITTU

161
00:13:55,061 --> 00:13:56,341
Stand at the front, Vivek.

162
00:13:56,461 --> 00:13:58,020
Bas, smear some
turmeric paste on her.

163
00:13:58,021 --> 00:13:59,181
Baskar…

164
00:13:59,301 --> 00:14:01,140
- You must do it.
- Do it properly!

165
00:14:01,141 --> 00:14:02,661
- That's enough.
- This guy…

166
00:14:02,781 --> 00:14:05,221
- Look at them blush!
- Aw, look how shy they are!

167
00:14:06,741 --> 00:14:08,941
Baskar, how are you doing?

168
00:14:09,461 --> 00:14:10,981
Yeah, I'm alright.

169
00:14:11,981 --> 00:14:15,301
- Seems like you got here last night?
- No, I just got here.

170
00:14:15,661 --> 00:14:17,260
- Oh, really?
- Yeah.

171
00:14:17,261 --> 00:14:19,820
I noticed your light
was still on past 11.

172
00:14:19,821 --> 00:14:22,621
So I assumed
you got on the last bus here.

173
00:14:23,494 --> 00:14:25,214
- Baskar!
- Excuse me…

174
00:14:25,741 --> 00:14:28,661
Something's fishy, Driver.

175
00:14:28,981 --> 00:14:30,701
Why would you talk to him?

176
00:14:30,821 --> 00:14:33,821
Like I wanted to.

177
00:14:40,781 --> 00:14:43,821
- How are you doing, Selvi?
- Uh… I'm well.

178
00:14:44,421 --> 00:14:47,581
I've been getting a lot of
alliances from IT--

179
00:14:48,021 --> 00:14:49,661
The nerve of you
to bring up alliances here!

180
00:14:49,861 --> 00:14:51,701
- Get me that mic!
- On it.

181
00:14:52,221 --> 00:14:53,381
Here you go.

182
00:14:54,061 --> 00:14:58,781
Listen up, everybody!
You too, broker.

183
00:14:58,981 --> 00:15:01,541
I have three sisters.

184
00:15:02,701 --> 00:15:05,421
Since Selvi's the only sibling
with two sons,

185
00:15:06,141 --> 00:15:08,501
one of them will definitely
be my son-in-law.

186
00:15:08,741 --> 00:15:12,141
If anyone comes to her,

187
00:15:12,261 --> 00:15:15,821
asking for their hands in marriage,
I will murder them.

188
00:15:15,981 --> 00:15:18,861
I say this with all due respect.
Thank you for listening.

189
00:15:19,701 --> 00:15:21,981
What's wrong with Uncle, Mom?

190
00:15:30,541 --> 00:15:33,261
Hey, ask her where she went.

191
00:15:33,741 --> 00:15:37,021
Why meddle in others’ affairs
when you’ve got your own?

192
00:15:37,341 --> 00:15:39,021
- Selvi, um…
- Yeah?

193
00:15:39,261 --> 00:15:41,301
- Getting back from Sankarapuram, is it?
- Yeah.

194
00:15:41,501 --> 00:15:44,060
I tried to apply for a widow pension.

195
00:15:44,061 --> 00:15:45,701
But the broker wants a 10,000 bribe.

196
00:15:45,861 --> 00:15:48,180
Ten thousand!
Such thievery!

197
00:15:48,181 --> 00:15:50,341
The gall of robbing the poor.

198
00:15:50,941 --> 00:15:55,540
If that tiny pension
is all they have to depend on,

199
00:15:55,541 --> 00:15:57,781
why not pay it up front
and get it over with?

200
00:16:00,541 --> 00:16:02,661
What makes you think
I’ll depend only on that?

201
00:16:03,421 --> 00:16:05,421
Can't a woman like me remarry?

202
00:16:05,821 --> 00:16:08,781
Like I want to die alone
in the end.

203
00:16:11,341 --> 00:16:12,341
Loser.

204
00:16:15,501 --> 00:16:16,420
Selvi?

205
00:16:16,421 --> 00:16:18,381
- Oh, Sir! Come in.
- Selvi.

206
00:16:18,941 --> 00:16:20,141
Can you please stitch
the flag corners?

207
00:16:20,501 --> 00:16:21,581
- Sure, sir. I'll--
- Actually…

208
00:16:22,221 --> 00:16:23,301
You can give it to me tomorrow.

209
00:16:23,421 --> 00:16:24,621
Okay, sir.

210
00:16:27,101 --> 00:16:28,141
Selvi…

211
00:16:28,981 --> 00:16:29,981
Yes, sir?

212
00:16:31,021 --> 00:16:32,661
You…

213
00:16:33,461 --> 00:16:34,381
Do you really…

214
00:16:36,021 --> 00:16:37,541
Do you really want to
get married again?

215
00:16:37,941 --> 00:16:41,020
Did you hear me talking
to Pachaperumal?

216
00:16:41,021 --> 00:16:43,861
No!
I'm just curious.

217
00:16:44,581 --> 00:16:45,501
Sir…

218
00:16:48,901 --> 00:16:52,741
I’ve loved having mehendi stains
on my hands since I was a child.

219
00:16:54,221 --> 00:16:56,101
I also love bindis.

220
00:16:56,621 --> 00:16:59,061
But now… I'm not supposed to
like any of these.

221
00:17:00,181 --> 00:17:01,181
Because…

222
00:17:01,381 --> 00:17:02,701
I'm a widow.

223
00:17:03,261 --> 00:17:06,421
I can go to the grove
only when Vimala wants to pee.

224
00:17:07,821 --> 00:17:09,821
If I go alone, people will talk.

225
00:17:12,021 --> 00:17:14,021
Rats run all night.
If I switch on the lights to catch them,

226
00:17:15,061 --> 00:17:18,620
people question why a house
without a man needs lights at night.

227
00:17:18,981 --> 00:17:21,340
I feel… like I'm in a prison.

228
00:17:25,821 --> 00:17:27,261
Even if I had killed my husband,

229
00:17:28,021 --> 00:17:30,301
it'll only be 10 or 12 years in prison.

230
00:17:31,861 --> 00:17:34,821
But my husband died
because of his ill fate,

231
00:17:36,101 --> 00:17:37,941
and I'm imprisoned for life.

232
00:17:39,101 --> 00:17:40,661
If one slipper is torn,

233
00:17:41,701 --> 00:17:43,421
the other one is also punished.

234
00:17:43,661 --> 00:17:44,701
To throw me out

235
00:17:45,341 --> 00:17:46,701
on the road like that…

236
00:17:48,141 --> 00:17:50,061
Am I just a slipper?

237
00:17:53,541 --> 00:17:54,981
My life…

238
00:17:55,941 --> 00:17:59,781
I can’t accept that
it has ended halfway like this.

239
00:18:02,621 --> 00:18:03,861
Like everyone,

240
00:18:04,901 --> 00:18:06,421
I, too, add salt to my food.

241
00:18:09,901 --> 00:18:10,781
Just like them…

242
00:18:12,301 --> 00:18:13,461
I, too…

243
00:18:16,021 --> 00:18:17,541
want to live a happy life.

244
00:18:21,141 --> 00:18:22,621
Why are you laughing?

245
00:18:24,141 --> 00:18:27,060
Do I look disgusting now?

246
00:18:27,061 --> 00:18:27,821
Oh, no!

247
00:18:27,981 --> 00:18:29,821
If someone had asked me
if I wanted to remarry,

248
00:18:29,941 --> 00:18:31,781
I'd just say 'yes.'
Just one word.

249
00:18:31,901 --> 00:18:35,301
But you women… have to
explain and justify so much.

250
00:18:36,941 --> 00:18:37,901
Sir…

251
00:18:38,421 --> 00:18:40,581
My sons have grown up.

252
00:18:41,941 --> 00:18:43,301
If they accept,

253
00:18:44,781 --> 00:18:46,461
I'd like to get married again.

254
00:18:51,421 --> 00:18:52,420
Good morning, ma'am!

255
00:18:52,421 --> 00:18:53,780
- GOVERMENT-AIDED PRIMARY SCHOOL
- Good morning, Baskar.

256
00:18:53,781 --> 00:18:55,420
- Hello, Baskar. Has Vivek come along?
- Good morning, sir.

257
00:18:55,421 --> 00:18:57,100
He left last night, sir.

258
00:18:57,101 --> 00:18:58,380
I'm on semester leave for a week.

259
00:18:58,381 --> 00:19:00,261
Mom asked me to drop this off.

260
00:19:00,821 --> 00:19:03,061
Arasi, put this in the cupboard, please.

261
00:19:03,701 --> 00:19:05,821
- See you, Ma'am.
- Baskar, just a minute!

262
00:19:06,301 --> 00:19:07,221
Hey, read it out loud!

263
00:19:07,701 --> 00:19:10,181
Nothing urgent.
Just wanted to talk to you.

264
00:19:10,821 --> 00:19:13,861
- Thing is… I, uh…
- Tell me, sir.

265
00:19:15,421 --> 00:19:16,781
Baskar, I…

266
00:19:17,421 --> 00:19:20,821
My friend's a teacher
at a government school in Kallakurichi.

267
00:19:21,861 --> 00:19:24,501
It's been about… two years
since his wife passed.

268
00:19:25,061 --> 00:19:26,861
He's a good man.
Can we…

269
00:19:27,581 --> 00:19:28,981
get Mom married to him?

270
00:19:38,061 --> 00:19:39,261
I already asked her.

271
00:19:45,061 --> 00:19:47,501
She asked me to check with you.

272
00:20:04,621 --> 00:20:05,701
Baskar?

273
00:20:10,461 --> 00:20:11,701
Baskar?

274
00:20:11,941 --> 00:20:13,461
What do you say?

275
00:20:14,101 --> 00:20:15,901
Pass the ball, Bas!

276
00:20:16,901 --> 00:20:18,941
- I'm coming!
- Come, come!

277
00:20:19,101 --> 00:20:20,741
Come on.

278
00:20:21,181 --> 00:20:22,901
Catch! Catch!

279
00:20:23,061 --> 00:20:24,500
Come on, just bowl!

280
00:20:24,501 --> 00:20:26,900
- Catch the ball!
- Come on, bowl!

281
00:20:26,901 --> 00:20:29,621
- I'm off to work. Watch the house.
- Ah, okay.

282
00:20:37,101 --> 00:20:40,221
That evening, when I
was on my way home from work,

283
00:20:40,381 --> 00:20:41,661
my heart was beating so fast.

284
00:20:42,661 --> 00:20:45,501
As a mother, I felt embarassed…

285
00:20:46,061 --> 00:20:48,541
to meet my son.

286
00:20:48,901 --> 00:20:50,181
Do you want tea?

287
00:20:51,821 --> 00:20:52,621
No.

288
00:20:59,621 --> 00:21:00,981
Uh… Baskar…

289
00:21:01,221 --> 00:21:04,181
I left the job at the travel company.
I'm thinking of working in Kerala.

290
00:21:04,861 --> 00:21:06,501
They are paying 15,000 per month.

291
00:21:06,701 --> 00:21:08,221
- And?
- There…

292
00:21:09,101 --> 00:21:13,341
Megala said she’s found
a job as a maid for me.

293
00:21:15,661 --> 00:21:17,021
What's with that look, man?

294
00:21:17,541 --> 00:21:19,061
Don't you want me
to go to Kerala?

295
00:21:20,661 --> 00:21:24,541
The travel company owner
has sent you riyals.

296
00:21:26,181 --> 00:21:29,501
It's in my purse.
I'll give it to you.

297
00:21:32,501 --> 00:21:35,381
Are you… angry with me?

298
00:21:36,501 --> 00:21:37,301
No.

299
00:21:38,661 --> 00:21:39,501
Don't lie to me.

300
00:21:40,141 --> 00:21:41,980
Look at yourself in the mirror.

301
00:21:41,981 --> 00:21:42,941
LOOK AT YOURSELF FIRST!

302
00:21:43,221 --> 00:21:44,981
You're telling me, huh?

303
00:21:45,781 --> 00:21:46,621
Here, look at yourself.

304
00:21:47,421 --> 00:21:48,381
Take a good look.

305
00:22:02,021 --> 00:22:05,541
♪ Your words
They stung me like a scorpion ♪

306
00:22:05,701 --> 00:22:08,421
♪ To whom do I go and cry? ♪

307
00:22:09,221 --> 00:22:12,701
♪ You took away my dreams ♪

308
00:22:12,941 --> 00:22:15,501
♪ Whom do I have now
To lay down my sorrows? ♪

309
00:22:16,861 --> 00:22:18,581
Time's up.
Give that to me, Baskar.

310
00:22:24,541 --> 00:22:26,381
Hey… What is this?

311
00:22:27,181 --> 00:22:29,101
You could've left after the first bell.

312
00:22:30,301 --> 00:22:33,821
If it had been any other exam,
I would’ve left.

313
00:22:34,501 --> 00:22:38,380
♪ Is it right or wrong
I'm wallowing by myself ♪

314
00:22:38,381 --> 00:22:41,620
♪ There are waves of anger
And waves of sorrow ♪

315
00:22:41,621 --> 00:22:45,620
♪ What's this madness?
I don't understand this confusion ♪

316
00:22:45,621 --> 00:22:49,221
♪ Oh, why do you cause me pain
I'm starting to hate you ♪

317
00:22:49,501 --> 00:22:53,180
♪ She taught me life's good and bad ♪

318
00:22:53,181 --> 00:22:56,421
♪ Why is she making these mistakes? ♪

319
00:22:56,701 --> 00:23:00,380
♪ She made a withered leaf
Win against the storm ♪

320
00:23:00,381 --> 00:23:03,581
♪ Why did she have to shatter me? ♪

321
00:23:03,741 --> 00:23:08,781
♪ When the rain stops, umbrella's a pain
I understand that ♪

322
00:23:11,021 --> 00:23:15,781
♪ I'll go as long as life takes me
These tears never stop ♪

323
00:23:26,741 --> 00:23:29,621
SANKARAPURAM, KALLAKURICHI

324
00:24:02,141 --> 00:24:03,260
- [in Malayalam] Who?
- Who was that?

325
00:24:03,261 --> 00:24:04,300
- Who was that?
- Selvi!

326
00:24:04,301 --> 00:24:06,861
Selvi?
Close the door.

327
00:24:10,661 --> 00:24:17,221
♪ Dreams, as long as they stay within
Don't cause pain ♪

328
00:24:17,901 --> 00:24:24,381
♪ I suffer so much,
Yet happiness never comes near ♪

329
00:24:25,101 --> 00:24:31,781
♪ No one chooses to be born a woman ♪

330
00:24:32,381 --> 00:24:38,621
♪ She rarely gets the life she wants ♪

331
00:24:39,181 --> 00:24:43,101
♪ I don't understand these laws ♪

332
00:24:43,301 --> 00:24:49,821
♪ Your words and action, they maybe right
My heart can't take it ♪

333
00:24:50,621 --> 00:24:54,181
♪ My heart and soul
They are scarred ♪

334
00:24:54,381 --> 00:24:57,461
♪ These eyes,
They forgot sleep ♪

335
00:24:57,621 --> 00:25:00,981
♪ Your words
They stung me like a scorpion ♪

336
00:25:01,301 --> 00:25:04,061
♪ To whom do I go and cry ♪

337
00:25:04,701 --> 00:25:08,141
♪ You took away my dreams ♪

338
00:25:08,421 --> 00:25:11,301
♪ Whom do I have now
To lay down my sorrows ♪

339
00:25:12,101 --> 00:25:13,341
Brother, this is from your mother.

340
00:25:17,981 --> 00:25:19,021
Do you want the bill?

341
00:25:19,581 --> 00:25:21,301
- Keep the change.
- Okay.

342
00:25:27,061 --> 00:25:28,901
Bro, what currency is this?

343
00:25:29,341 --> 00:25:30,981
Get the money ready.
I'll come get it.

344
00:25:34,301 --> 00:25:38,781
This isn’t a bindi.
It’s a full stop to everything.

345
00:25:39,061 --> 00:25:40,101
Study well.

346
00:25:42,061 --> 00:25:45,061
After that,
I got serious about my studies.

347
00:25:45,781 --> 00:25:49,261
After college, I didn’t want
an engineering job.

348
00:25:49,981 --> 00:25:53,821
So I started an IELTS coaching center.
It’s doing well.

349
00:25:55,781 --> 00:25:57,301
FIVE YEARS LATER

350
00:25:59,301 --> 00:26:00,101
Are you Hari?

351
00:26:00,461 --> 00:26:01,661
- Are you Anu?
- To Ulundurpettai.

352
00:26:02,541 --> 00:26:04,020
- Get in.
- Bro…

353
00:26:04,021 --> 00:26:05,261
Two tickets to Kallakurichi.

354
00:26:05,421 --> 00:26:07,021
We only have sleeper seats.
Will you take it?

355
00:26:10,581 --> 00:26:11,821
Anyone for Karuvathur?

356
00:26:14,981 --> 00:26:16,221
Be careful.

357
00:26:16,381 --> 00:26:19,141
Mind your head.
Hear you go.

358
00:26:38,141 --> 00:26:39,861
[phone ringing]

359
00:26:40,861 --> 00:26:41,820
Sandhya.

360
00:26:41,821 --> 00:26:43,461
- Pick up your phone.
- Just stay silent.

361
00:26:44,301 --> 00:26:45,701
Hello, Mom?

362
00:26:48,181 --> 00:26:50,381
How dare you sleep with him?

363
00:26:50,781 --> 00:26:52,821
- You can't do whatever you want.
- Answer her.

364
00:26:52,941 --> 00:26:55,260
- I sent you to college to study.
- What's his name? Tell me.

365
00:26:55,261 --> 00:26:56,261
Answer me now!

366
00:27:15,301 --> 00:27:16,421
Are you Selvi?

367
00:27:16,861 --> 00:27:17,741
Yes.

368
00:27:31,501 --> 00:27:33,300
My mom is here.
She's furious.

369
00:27:33,301 --> 00:27:34,861
Hang up, Sandhya.
I'll call you later.

370
00:27:40,501 --> 00:27:41,901
To hell with this spinach.

371
00:27:49,981 --> 00:27:52,501
We didn't know
it was a sleeper bus, Selvi.

372
00:27:53,101 --> 00:27:58,341
And just because it was a sleeper bus
doesn’t mean we slept together.

373
00:28:00,021 --> 00:28:01,141
What are you even saying?

374
00:28:01,461 --> 00:28:03,460
- How dare you talk like that--
- Mom, no!

375
00:28:03,461 --> 00:28:04,380
It's not what you think.

376
00:28:04,381 --> 00:28:06,140
We didn't lie down.
We sat with the laptop,

377
00:28:06,141 --> 00:28:07,820
and worked on our project.

378
00:28:07,821 --> 00:28:10,020
That's it.
Stop looking at me like that.

379
00:28:10,021 --> 00:28:11,701
We know our limits, Selvi.

380
00:28:11,941 --> 00:28:14,501
To hell with your limits!

381
00:28:14,741 --> 00:28:16,421
That woman threw your shoes
and is warning me,

382
00:28:16,581 --> 00:28:19,221
that you won't have legs
if you go behind her daughter.

383
00:28:19,461 --> 00:28:21,381
Gosh! Don't get scared over all that.

384
00:28:22,941 --> 00:28:24,661
- What does he expect?
- Selvi…

385
00:28:26,021 --> 00:28:26,901
Gosh!

386
00:28:28,021 --> 00:28:30,900
Do you think I’d follow her
if she didn’t like me?

387
00:28:30,901 --> 00:28:31,741
Huh?

388
00:28:32,141 --> 00:28:32,941
Also,

389
00:28:33,661 --> 00:28:36,941
you taught us not to even look at a girl
if she doesn’t like it.

390
00:28:37,181 --> 00:28:38,781
Selvi, you're a superb mom.

391
00:28:45,901 --> 00:28:47,341
What's her name again?

392
00:28:47,701 --> 00:28:48,861
- Huh?
- Tell me.

393
00:28:50,021 --> 00:28:50,901
Sandhya.

394
00:28:51,141 --> 00:28:52,141
How long have you known her?

395
00:28:53,021 --> 00:28:54,261
Since our first year.

396
00:28:55,381 --> 00:28:57,741
High… since high school.

397
00:28:58,301 --> 00:29:00,301
You better tell me the truth.

398
00:29:01,621 --> 00:29:06,381
She studied in our school
till fifth grade.

399
00:29:07,021 --> 00:29:09,061
- Since then.
- You thief!

400
00:29:09,621 --> 00:29:10,501
Right here?

401
00:29:10,781 --> 00:29:12,181
Since elementary?!

402
00:29:13,781 --> 00:29:16,261
You did all this right under my nose!

403
00:29:19,341 --> 00:29:20,221
God!

404
00:29:20,741 --> 00:29:23,541
What will I even tell your uncle?

405
00:29:24,181 --> 00:29:25,861
That's your problem now?

406
00:29:26,501 --> 00:29:28,781
Go. Tell your favorite son.

407
00:29:28,981 --> 00:29:29,821
Leave me alone.

408
00:29:30,261 --> 00:29:31,301
I'll kill you. Get lost.

409
00:29:31,701 --> 00:29:33,941
- Do whatever you want.
- Marry your son off soon.

410
00:29:34,061 --> 00:29:35,740
I'm definitely leaving this place.

411
00:29:35,741 --> 00:29:38,020
Where will you even go
at this age?

412
00:29:38,021 --> 00:29:39,861
It's not… what you think.

413
00:29:40,061 --> 00:29:41,301
When is Baskar getting married?

414
00:29:43,581 --> 00:29:46,341
Yeah, it's his marriage
I'm thinking about.

415
00:29:47,581 --> 00:29:50,221
Our second-born has brought trouble.

416
00:29:50,701 --> 00:29:54,061
It's not like Baskar will agree
to marry Chittu.

417
00:29:54,661 --> 00:29:56,461
How am I going to get through all this?

418
00:29:56,581 --> 00:29:58,140
Tell me a way.

419
00:29:58,141 --> 00:29:59,741
You keep rotating all the time.

420
00:30:00,061 --> 00:30:02,181
[phone rings]

421
00:30:03,981 --> 00:30:04,821
Baskar!

422
00:30:05,061 --> 00:30:06,541
- Mom?
- Hundred years, darling.

423
00:30:06,701 --> 00:30:08,221
- Really?
- Yeah.

424
00:30:08,421 --> 00:30:09,381
I was just thinking about you.

425
00:30:09,941 --> 00:30:11,301
Did you eat?

426
00:30:11,821 --> 00:30:13,861
What?! Did I eat?

427
00:30:14,301 --> 00:30:16,861
Looks like it's going to rain.

428
00:30:17,621 --> 00:30:18,421
Mom…

429
00:30:19,061 --> 00:30:21,740
Did you cook something,
or is it just black coffee as usual?

430
00:30:21,741 --> 00:30:24,461
I’d have had black coffee if I were alone.
But Vivek’s here.

431
00:30:24,781 --> 00:30:26,181
Yeah, he told me.

432
00:30:29,821 --> 00:30:30,661
Mom…

433
00:30:31,501 --> 00:30:34,621
I… I have something to tell you.

434
00:30:34,741 --> 00:30:35,581
What is it?

435
00:30:35,861 --> 00:30:37,341
Do you need money?

436
00:30:37,701 --> 00:30:40,221
Come on, Mom.
I'm earning now.

437
00:30:40,861 --> 00:30:41,981
Alright. Tell me.

438
00:30:42,421 --> 00:30:43,261
It's…

439
00:30:43,981 --> 00:30:47,101
- I've been talking to my friends.
- About what?

440
00:30:47,661 --> 00:30:49,021
You are alone.

441
00:30:49,661 --> 00:30:51,021
So, I thought…

442
00:30:51,621 --> 00:30:52,901
Why don't you…

443
00:30:53,421 --> 00:30:55,181
get married again?

444
00:31:15,101 --> 00:31:18,421
Why don't you…
get married again?

445
00:31:26,701 --> 00:31:27,621
Okay, hold on.

446
00:31:29,581 --> 00:31:30,621
Mom, your son is calling.

447
00:31:30,741 --> 00:31:32,500
Talk to him and get the marriage fixed,

448
00:31:32,501 --> 00:31:34,021
for him, not me.

449
00:31:34,541 --> 00:31:36,620
- Mom!
- Why are you blabbering like this?

450
00:31:36,621 --> 00:31:38,341
Have you gone mad?

451
00:31:38,461 --> 00:31:39,421
Why are you shouting now?

452
00:31:39,541 --> 00:31:43,500
When you called me,
I thought you had changed.

453
00:31:43,501 --> 00:31:45,781
Now I know.
You've lost your mind.

454
00:31:46,101 --> 00:31:47,861
Mom, just think about it.

455
00:31:48,061 --> 00:31:49,381
Don't make me talk.

456
00:31:49,501 --> 00:31:51,741
Go do your work.
You idiot!

457
00:31:58,701 --> 00:32:02,381
If you're going to bring it up again,
don't call me.

458
00:32:02,541 --> 00:32:04,261
I'll forget that I ever had you.

459
00:32:04,381 --> 00:32:06,981
Mom, it was you
who talked about this to Sir.

460
00:32:07,421 --> 00:32:10,181
I did have an idea then.
Now, I don't.

461
00:32:10,461 --> 00:32:13,221
I'm 42.
Half my head is white.

462
00:32:13,501 --> 00:32:14,621
I've even started dyeing my hair.

463
00:32:14,781 --> 00:32:17,461
You are wasting your time.
And the entire village will spit at me.

464
00:32:17,701 --> 00:32:20,661
So it’s the villagers you’re afraid of.
But you are interested, right?

465
00:32:20,781 --> 00:32:23,101
Don't talk rubbish,
sitting comfortably in Coimbatore.

466
00:32:23,301 --> 00:32:25,461
Come here and try living my life
for a day.

467
00:32:25,581 --> 00:32:28,621
Who will marry you
if I get married at this age?

468
00:32:28,781 --> 00:32:31,141
- I'll take care of my marriage.
- Oh.

469
00:32:31,261 --> 00:32:34,261
- Does Vivek know about this?
- Just say the word.

470
00:32:34,381 --> 00:32:35,461
I'll talk to him.

471
00:32:38,141 --> 00:32:41,021
[phone rings]

472
00:32:41,341 --> 00:32:42,541
So, what does the groom do?

473
00:32:42,701 --> 00:32:46,140
He's in construction.
So, when are you getting married?

474
00:32:46,141 --> 00:32:47,381
Mom, when's the wedding?

475
00:32:49,341 --> 00:32:50,421
I'll kill you.

476
00:32:52,381 --> 00:32:54,581
Selvi, shall we tie the next
banana tree in your house?

477
00:32:55,261 --> 00:32:59,741
This moron keeps yapping
without knowing anything!

478
00:33:00,181 --> 00:33:01,301
Why are you laughing?

479
00:33:01,461 --> 00:33:03,181
You can't play with my life like this.

480
00:33:03,901 --> 00:33:06,701
Do you have a life to play with?

481
00:33:10,381 --> 00:33:11,221
Selvi.

482
00:33:11,621 --> 00:33:13,141
Sandhya's people are torturing her.

483
00:33:13,421 --> 00:33:15,221
They are sending her to college
just for the exams.

484
00:33:15,341 --> 00:33:17,140
So? What are you trying to say?

485
00:33:17,141 --> 00:33:17,981
Selvi, it's…

486
00:33:19,141 --> 00:33:22,021
When are you planning
Baskar's marriage?

487
00:33:27,621 --> 00:33:29,581
Hey, Vivek's in a problem.

488
00:33:30,061 --> 00:33:31,541
He can marry
only after you get married.

489
00:33:32,221 --> 00:33:33,421
Shall I start looking for a girl?

490
00:33:33,741 --> 00:33:36,261
Mom, you can get him married
whenever you want.

491
00:33:37,541 --> 00:33:38,861
But my wedding…

492
00:33:41,141 --> 00:33:42,501
Listen to me carefully.

493
00:33:43,221 --> 00:33:47,301
I’ll get married the same day,
right after you do.

494
00:33:47,741 --> 00:33:49,581
Otherwisw, I'll never get married.

495
00:33:49,861 --> 00:33:50,901
Hey, listen.

496
00:34:01,341 --> 00:34:03,421
Hey, new bride!
How are you?

497
00:34:03,581 --> 00:34:05,861
- I’m good.
- All good on the groom’s side?

498
00:34:06,021 --> 00:34:07,900
- It's alright. Atleast for now.
- Hope it stays that way.

499
00:34:07,901 --> 00:34:08,901
All thanks to you.

500
00:34:09,101 --> 00:34:11,179
Know what matchmaker Moorthy’s
specialty is?

501
00:34:11,180 --> 00:34:13,220
I don’t just seal the deal.

502
00:34:13,421 --> 00:34:15,340
I stick around for
the after service, too.

503
00:34:15,341 --> 00:34:16,780
- How are you?
- Hello, Selvi.

504
00:34:16,781 --> 00:34:17,740
I'll hang up.

505
00:34:17,901 --> 00:34:19,501
So, what’s the occasion?

506
00:34:19,660 --> 00:34:21,659
You know why we've come to see you.
Here.

507
00:34:21,660 --> 00:34:22,621
Lord Muruga!

508
00:34:25,381 --> 00:34:28,220
If I find a girl for Baskar,
won’t your brother come after me?

509
00:34:28,421 --> 00:34:30,780
I’ll see to it.

510
00:34:30,781 --> 00:34:33,740
Not just you,
everyone will see me get ripped apart.

511
00:34:33,901 --> 00:34:35,259
Alright.
Tell me.

512
00:34:35,260 --> 00:34:38,100
- Should she be working, or--
- That’s not a concern.

513
00:34:38,101 --> 00:34:42,739
The moment he sees her,
he should want to marry her.

514
00:34:42,740 --> 00:34:45,020
- Get me a girl like that.
- Consider it done!

515
00:34:45,021 --> 00:34:46,740
So we’ll get this done soon, yeah?

516
00:34:47,581 --> 00:34:50,061
Madam, you just shared his picture.

517
00:34:50,260 --> 00:34:53,301
You can’t rush this
like sealing a water can.

518
00:34:53,421 --> 00:34:55,380
- We're talking about marriage!
- Okay, take care of it.

519
00:34:55,381 --> 00:34:57,340
But send him the photos today, okay?

520
00:34:57,341 --> 00:34:58,821
Huh? And?

521
00:34:59,861 --> 00:35:00,861
Really, Mom?

522
00:35:01,021 --> 00:35:02,021
Yes.

523
00:35:02,221 --> 00:35:03,821
I’ll get married.

524
00:35:03,941 --> 00:35:07,221
But first, you’ll get some photos
from the matchmaker.

525
00:35:07,381 --> 00:35:08,501
Go through the girls’ photos.

526
00:35:08,661 --> 00:35:11,381
If any of them catch your eye,
talk to her parents.

527
00:35:11,501 --> 00:35:13,061
Tell them about our deal.
Alright?

528
00:35:13,221 --> 00:35:15,941
- What "our deal", Mom?
- What else?

529
00:35:16,181 --> 00:35:19,860
Tell them that, "I need to settle
my mom’s marriage first.

530
00:35:19,861 --> 00:35:21,861
Only after that can we marry."

531
00:35:22,221 --> 00:35:24,461
Alright? If they're okay with that,

532
00:35:28,461 --> 00:35:30,860
you can start finding me a match.

533
00:35:30,861 --> 00:35:32,101
You promise?

534
00:35:32,381 --> 00:35:33,781
Yes, I promise.

535
00:35:33,981 --> 00:35:35,701
Thanks, Mom!

536
00:35:43,141 --> 00:35:45,101
No dad’s going to agree to this!

537
00:35:45,941 --> 00:35:48,820
If Baskar ends up liking her,

538
00:35:48,821 --> 00:35:50,140
he won’t bother me anymore, right?

539
00:35:50,141 --> 00:35:54,060
They talk big about
their mom’s marriage

540
00:35:54,061 --> 00:35:55,941
until a pretty girl
catches their eye!

541
00:36:15,621 --> 00:36:16,741
Come in!

542
00:36:20,541 --> 00:36:21,581
Excuse me?

543
00:36:23,221 --> 00:36:24,181
Hello?

544
00:36:25,541 --> 00:36:26,781
Hello?

545
00:36:27,621 --> 00:36:28,781
Action!

546
00:36:28,901 --> 00:36:30,100
Surprise!

547
00:36:30,101 --> 00:36:32,460
Hey, darlings.
Welcome to the Kimki Channel.

548
00:36:32,461 --> 00:36:33,580
This is Baskar.

549
00:36:33,581 --> 00:36:36,301
You haven’t met
Baskar before, right?

550
00:36:36,581 --> 00:36:37,780
Guess what?

551
00:36:37,781 --> 00:36:39,661
We’re meeting Baskar
for the first time, too!

552
00:36:40,261 --> 00:36:41,101
Where are you running off to?

553
00:36:41,941 --> 00:36:43,741
In this video...
Get in here!

554
00:36:43,901 --> 00:36:47,020
You’ll get to know
who Baskar is and why he’s here.

555
00:36:47,021 --> 00:36:47,780
Cut!

556
00:36:47,781 --> 00:36:50,661
I'm Vandhana's mom
and he's her dad, Kimki.

557
00:36:51,141 --> 00:36:52,461
Hi! Welcome.

558
00:36:52,781 --> 00:36:56,981
Baskar, he’s the biggest fan
of Korean director Kim Ki-duk!

559
00:36:57,141 --> 00:36:58,021
Come.

560
00:36:58,701 --> 00:36:59,781
Make way for the groom!

561
00:37:01,581 --> 00:37:02,660
Hey, darlings!

562
00:37:02,661 --> 00:37:06,580
Meet Baskar. Groom No. 1,
Vandhana’s first match.

563
00:37:06,581 --> 00:37:09,500
- Baskar, don’t hide your face.
- Say hi to the viewers.

564
00:37:09,501 --> 00:37:10,740
- Please stop doing this.
- Baskar!

565
00:37:10,741 --> 00:37:13,140
You’ve got lakhs watching you!
Give us a smile.

566
00:37:13,141 --> 00:37:14,101
Sir!

567
00:37:14,301 --> 00:37:16,741
Did you mention she’s a YouTuber
in the matrimony profile?

568
00:37:16,901 --> 00:37:17,941
I can't talk here.

569
00:37:18,101 --> 00:37:19,741
Let me see the girl.
I’ll be on my way.

570
00:37:22,181 --> 00:37:25,500
Viewers, he’s really excited
to see his bride!

571
00:37:25,501 --> 00:37:28,541
He’ll tell us how it went
once he’s back.

572
00:37:28,661 --> 00:37:30,261
Vandhana's upstairs.
Go on.

573
00:37:33,061 --> 00:37:34,981
Really?
Okay, got it.

574
00:37:35,261 --> 00:37:36,261
Okay, Mom.

575
00:37:37,341 --> 00:37:38,381
I'll take care.

576
00:37:42,781 --> 00:37:44,741
Hi.
I'm Vandhana.

577
00:37:45,621 --> 00:37:46,741
Baskar.

578
00:37:52,741 --> 00:37:54,540
Baskar, your profile was interesting.

579
00:37:54,541 --> 00:37:56,621
A mechatronics degree,
and now IELTS coaching?

580
00:37:57,101 --> 00:37:58,141
How come?

581
00:37:59,701 --> 00:38:01,941
For my own professional satisfaction.

582
00:38:02,261 --> 00:38:03,141
I…

583
00:38:03,741 --> 00:38:04,741
Listen.

584
00:38:05,061 --> 00:38:09,581
I hate arranged marriages.
Feels like browsing and picking.

585
00:38:09,941 --> 00:38:11,421
Then why are you here?

586
00:38:11,581 --> 00:38:12,621
That is...

587
00:38:13,141 --> 00:38:15,501
I had to rethink things
because of my mom.

588
00:38:17,101 --> 00:38:18,141
Why?

589
00:38:19,181 --> 00:38:21,620
I can’t explain that now.
Sorry for taking up your time.

590
00:38:21,621 --> 00:38:22,941
I better get going.
I'm sorry.

591
00:38:23,341 --> 00:38:24,341
Hello!

592
00:38:25,301 --> 00:38:28,981
You come all the way here, say you hate
arranged marriages, and just leave?

593
00:38:30,821 --> 00:38:32,221
It's my fault.
Forgive me.

594
00:38:32,541 --> 00:38:35,461
I can’t stand all that shooting
setup down there!

595
00:38:35,861 --> 00:38:36,741
I should go.

596
00:38:37,381 --> 00:38:38,460
Excuse me!

597
00:38:38,461 --> 00:38:39,500
Baskar.

598
00:38:39,501 --> 00:38:43,421
You gave them roughly 90 seconds
of footage when you arrived, right?

599
00:38:44,141 --> 00:38:47,581
Before you even start your bike,
I’ll have everything uploaded!

600
00:38:47,741 --> 00:38:49,101
Mind it!

601
00:38:50,501 --> 00:38:53,141
Any idea how many subscribers
we’ve got?

602
00:38:53,581 --> 00:38:55,261
1.8 million.

603
00:38:57,181 --> 00:39:00,181
Even a 60-second clip of them talking

604
00:39:00,741 --> 00:39:02,061
can bring in big viewership.

605
00:39:02,741 --> 00:39:03,941
What are you going to do?

606
00:39:08,781 --> 00:39:11,941
So, when your mother
wanted to remarry,

607
00:39:12,621 --> 00:39:13,661
you were against it?

608
00:39:14,221 --> 00:39:15,021
Yes.

609
00:39:16,621 --> 00:39:18,421
So what led to your enlightenment?

610
00:39:22,101 --> 00:39:23,861
I brought my mother over to Coimbatore

611
00:39:24,221 --> 00:39:27,381
since she was all by herself
after I started my coaching center.

612
00:39:27,581 --> 00:39:30,901
I turned my old office into my home.

613
00:39:31,021 --> 00:39:33,541
Whenever I checked the CCTV,

614
00:39:33,661 --> 00:39:35,581
trapped inside four walls,

615
00:39:35,781 --> 00:39:38,061
she kept doing chores,
with no one to talk to.

616
00:39:38,221 --> 00:39:40,021
It really started weighing on me.

617
00:39:40,141 --> 00:39:41,661
Look, a rat’s trapped!

618
00:39:42,061 --> 00:39:43,141
Look!

619
00:39:44,421 --> 00:39:46,461
The way she stood there…

620
00:39:46,621 --> 00:39:50,141
she looked like a caged rat

621
00:39:50,301 --> 00:39:54,261
holding another rat in a trap.

622
00:39:56,301 --> 00:40:00,301
Guilt crept in,
like I’d ruined my mom’s life.

623
00:40:00,461 --> 00:40:02,381
I went to meet Sister Angela.

624
00:40:03,581 --> 00:40:05,861
So, now you feel guilty
about your mother, right?

625
00:40:06,941 --> 00:40:09,661
Baskar, let me answer
as a biology student.

626
00:40:10,861 --> 00:40:13,941
Every living human,

627
00:40:14,301 --> 00:40:17,181
or rather, any living being,
has primary needs.

628
00:40:17,341 --> 00:40:19,100
Basic needs.

629
00:40:19,101 --> 00:40:20,181
Know what that is?

630
00:40:21,461 --> 00:40:22,421
Eating.

631
00:40:22,701 --> 00:40:23,741
Sleeping.

632
00:40:24,301 --> 00:40:25,341
And the third is…

633
00:40:25,621 --> 00:40:27,061
Finding a partner.

634
00:40:27,501 --> 00:40:28,500
Right?

635
00:40:28,501 --> 00:40:32,181
Without the first two,
we can’t survive.

636
00:40:32,901 --> 00:40:34,141
And the third?

637
00:40:34,461 --> 00:40:35,461
Physical needs.

638
00:40:36,181 --> 00:40:39,341
Sure, we can live without it.

639
00:40:40,301 --> 00:40:41,661
But it’ll eat us up inside.

640
00:40:44,541 --> 00:40:46,821
That’s exactly why marriage exists.

641
00:40:50,661 --> 00:40:51,861
Sister, may I be frank?

642
00:40:52,101 --> 00:40:54,781
My mom is already 42.

643
00:40:55,581 --> 00:40:57,421
Do you think
she still wants to get married?

644
00:40:57,541 --> 00:40:58,901
It is optional, Baskar.

645
00:40:59,661 --> 00:41:01,821
We’re nuns.
We’ve chosen celibacy.

646
00:41:02,421 --> 00:41:04,781
We have a divine calling.
So we chose this path.

647
00:41:05,461 --> 00:41:08,901
But if your mother wants to marry,
that’s her call to make.

648
00:41:10,981 --> 00:41:13,501
Hey, stop rubbing your eye.
Close your eyes for a minute.

649
00:41:16,981 --> 00:41:17,901
And…

650
00:41:18,101 --> 00:41:23,861
Instead of just looking at someone
and wondering if he’s hungry,

651
00:41:24,301 --> 00:41:26,621
humanity is asking him
if he wants to eat.

652
00:41:27,861 --> 00:41:28,861
She's your mom.

653
00:41:29,581 --> 00:41:30,581
Try asking her that.

654
00:41:32,541 --> 00:41:35,181
Baskar?
Now, open your eyes.

655
00:41:39,341 --> 00:41:42,381
That day,
Sister truly opened my eyes.

656
00:41:42,661 --> 00:41:43,621
Wow.

657
00:41:44,701 --> 00:41:45,581
Superb.

658
00:41:46,541 --> 00:41:47,421
Amazing!

659
00:41:49,661 --> 00:41:53,021
Only then did I start talking
to my mom about marriage.

660
00:41:54,781 --> 00:41:55,661
Good job.

661
00:41:58,301 --> 00:41:59,581
Baskar, you know what?

662
00:41:59,821 --> 00:42:01,301
Even I hate this whole

663
00:42:01,501 --> 00:42:04,181
browsing-and-picking
arranged-marriage setup.

664
00:42:05,341 --> 00:42:06,421
Then why all this?

665
00:42:07,261 --> 00:42:11,221
My dad came up with this
to increase the subscriber count.

666
00:42:11,461 --> 00:42:14,661
He turned my matchmaking
into content.

667
00:42:23,581 --> 00:42:24,701
Alright.

668
00:42:25,021 --> 00:42:28,461
I need to find a girl to show my mom
and get her okay to remarry.

669
00:42:30,061 --> 00:42:32,061
And you’re looking for
matchmaking content.

670
00:42:33,781 --> 00:42:36,421
Then let’s make a deal
without telling our families.

671
00:42:37,861 --> 00:42:38,941
A fake drama.

672
00:42:40,061 --> 00:42:41,021
I don't get it.

673
00:42:41,621 --> 00:42:42,580
Action!

674
00:42:42,581 --> 00:42:45,781
Hi, Kimkis!
Baskar and I really clicked.

675
00:42:46,141 --> 00:42:50,341
Not just me,
even my mom and dad love Baskar!

676
00:42:50,461 --> 00:42:54,101
Comment below and tell us
what you think about us.

677
00:42:56,341 --> 00:42:57,940
She's indeed beautiful.

678
00:42:57,941 --> 00:43:00,940
But are they truly okay
with me remarrying?

679
00:43:00,941 --> 00:43:03,301
Mom, you promised!
Don’t back out now.

680
00:43:03,501 --> 00:43:04,941
Get dolled up
and wait inside.

681
00:43:05,101 --> 00:43:06,540
Manohar will be there tomorrow
to take your photos.

682
00:43:06,541 --> 00:43:07,700
For the matrimonial profile.

683
00:43:07,701 --> 00:43:08,701
I'll hang up.

684
00:43:14,261 --> 00:43:15,981
COIMBATORE

685
00:43:25,661 --> 00:43:27,661
Hey, what’s with the sudden visit?

686
00:43:32,301 --> 00:43:34,461
Vivek. Hey!
Get up.

687
00:43:37,901 --> 00:43:38,901
Have this.

688
00:43:42,341 --> 00:43:43,741
What's wrong, man?

689
00:43:44,981 --> 00:43:46,781
Vivek, what was that for?

690
00:43:47,061 --> 00:43:48,181
What's up with you?

691
00:43:48,461 --> 00:43:50,021
Why are you bothering Mom?

692
00:43:50,661 --> 00:43:52,581
Oh, so this is how
she’s doing things now?

693
00:43:52,901 --> 00:43:54,661
Of course she’ll come to me.
What about it?

694
00:43:55,141 --> 00:43:56,460
Is she uncomfortable with marriage,

695
00:43:56,461 --> 00:43:58,301
or is it getting in your way?

696
00:43:59,261 --> 00:44:01,461
Yes, it’s affecting my marriage.

697
00:44:01,621 --> 00:44:03,741
Did mother pressure you
to get her remarried?

698
00:44:03,941 --> 00:44:06,221
Did she? Did she?
Tell me!

699
00:44:06,341 --> 00:44:09,421
She did.
At the age of 35!

700
00:44:10,541 --> 00:44:11,340
How dare you?

701
00:44:11,341 --> 00:44:13,461
How can you even imagine
another man in his place?

702
00:44:16,421 --> 00:44:18,581
Won’t you ever think about Mom?

703
00:44:19,421 --> 00:44:20,821
Mom is still alive.

704
00:44:23,581 --> 00:44:25,061
She’s not interested
in marriage at this age.

705
00:44:25,461 --> 00:44:27,620
Drop it.
I’ll take care of her like a queen.

706
00:44:27,621 --> 00:44:28,620
As if!

707
00:44:28,621 --> 00:44:30,221
We only go home twice.

708
00:44:30,421 --> 00:44:31,740
Even then, we’re glued to our phone

709
00:44:31,741 --> 00:44:32,980
or talking to someone else.

710
00:44:32,981 --> 00:44:35,221
Do we ever sit
and talk to Mom properly?

711
00:44:35,861 --> 00:44:36,820
This guy, I swear!

712
00:44:36,821 --> 00:44:38,900
You pass your broken phone to Mom,

713
00:44:38,901 --> 00:44:40,220
and you claim you’ll
treat her like a queen?

714
00:44:40,221 --> 00:44:42,061
Do we even know her number?
Look!

715
00:44:42,581 --> 00:44:44,381
She has a life of her own.

716
00:44:44,581 --> 00:44:46,021
It’s not for us to decide.

717
00:44:46,221 --> 00:44:47,820
This is pure exploitation, man!

718
00:44:47,821 --> 00:44:49,181
In the name of mother's love…

719
00:44:58,221 --> 00:44:59,740
Do you expect every son

720
00:44:59,741 --> 00:45:01,740
to ask his widowed mother
if she wants to remarry?

721
00:45:01,741 --> 00:45:02,820
- Tell me!
- Yes!

722
00:45:02,821 --> 00:45:03,981
They should!

723
00:45:05,101 --> 00:45:06,661
They should, man!
They should.

724
00:45:06,901 --> 00:45:08,660
Like our mom,
who was widowed at 25.

725
00:45:08,661 --> 00:45:10,381
Even at the age of 40 or 50,

726
00:45:10,661 --> 00:45:12,380
her son, daughters,

727
00:45:12,381 --> 00:45:15,181
heck even her father
should ask her if she wants to remarry.

728
00:45:17,261 --> 00:45:18,221
Listen.

729
00:45:18,421 --> 00:45:20,141
Feels like I’m looking at myself
from four years ago.

730
00:45:21,501 --> 00:45:23,621
It'll take another four years
for you to realize all this.

731
00:45:23,941 --> 00:45:26,660
By the time we’ll get old…
God, I can’t wait that long.

732
00:45:26,661 --> 00:45:27,541
You leave.

733
00:45:29,301 --> 00:45:31,020
Won't you just drop it?

734
00:45:31,021 --> 00:45:33,261
- Won't you?
- I won't, damn it!

735
00:45:36,141 --> 00:45:37,621
Let me go!

736
00:45:38,101 --> 00:45:38,981
I'll just--

737
00:45:39,221 --> 00:45:40,941
[phone rings]

738
00:45:45,261 --> 00:45:46,941
Write it.
In big letters.

739
00:45:47,061 --> 00:45:49,941
- Go on.
- Big enough to scream shame.

740
00:45:50,061 --> 00:45:51,661
It's time she knew our power.

741
00:45:52,421 --> 00:45:55,021
- Who’s writing on my walls?
- Here she is!

742
00:45:55,181 --> 00:45:56,660
- Smack him.
- Back off!

743
00:45:56,661 --> 00:45:58,501
- Hey, Selvi!
- Pachaperumal!

744
00:45:58,701 --> 00:46:00,261
Why are you just standing there?

745
00:46:00,741 --> 00:46:01,821
Who is he?

746
00:46:02,221 --> 00:46:04,580
He’s the financier
who gave you the money.

747
00:46:04,581 --> 00:46:05,420
Listen!

748
00:46:05,421 --> 00:46:07,780
After all the debts
your husband left behind,

749
00:46:07,781 --> 00:46:09,220
you came to my finance company,

750
00:46:09,221 --> 00:46:11,420
saying you didn’t even have
money for your kids’ studies

751
00:46:11,421 --> 00:46:15,101
and held my partner’s feet and begged!
You’ve forgotten, huh?

752
00:46:15,541 --> 00:46:18,180
Selling this house won’t even
cover the interest.

753
00:46:18,181 --> 00:46:19,181
How long has it been, huh?

754
00:46:19,661 --> 00:46:21,620
You send reminder letters, don’t you?

755
00:46:21,621 --> 00:46:23,100
You’re supposed to put up a notice.

756
00:46:23,101 --> 00:46:24,621
Instead, you’re scribbling on walls?

757
00:46:24,861 --> 00:46:27,541
If you delay payment,
not just on the walls,

758
00:46:27,861 --> 00:46:29,421
they’ll write on you, too.

759
00:46:29,581 --> 00:46:32,341
I heard you went to a financier
for your kids’ studies?

760
00:46:32,541 --> 00:46:34,821
Why worry?
I'm here for you.

761
00:46:37,101 --> 00:46:38,541
Hey!
Look--

762
00:46:49,941 --> 00:46:51,980
I won't go easy on you!

763
00:46:51,981 --> 00:46:55,700
You deface my walls,
and you dare raise your voice?

764
00:46:55,701 --> 00:46:56,980
Have you lost your senses?

765
00:46:56,981 --> 00:46:59,581
Pachaperumal is all red now!

766
00:47:18,421 --> 00:47:20,300
Why haven't you done
anything about this?

767
00:47:20,301 --> 00:47:22,141
- You could've painted over it.
- Come in, brother?

768
00:47:22,261 --> 00:47:23,101
Welcome, Uncle.

769
00:47:23,781 --> 00:47:25,860
We've paid them back, Uncle.
They said they'll send their men.

770
00:47:25,861 --> 00:47:26,821
Let them remove it.

771
00:47:27,101 --> 00:47:29,221
I just stopped by at Pachaperumal's
to yell at him.

772
00:47:29,541 --> 00:47:31,541
He's rambling about calling
for a meeting, it seems.

773
00:47:32,781 --> 00:47:34,421
Like he would.

774
00:47:34,701 --> 00:47:37,941
He’s still a snake,
waiting to strike again.

775
00:47:38,101 --> 00:47:40,221
Vivek, serve Uncle his coffee.

776
00:47:41,741 --> 00:47:43,941
What happened at Coimbatore?
Did you talk?

777
00:47:44,061 --> 00:47:45,221
What did he say?

778
00:47:45,781 --> 00:47:46,740
I'll tell you.

779
00:47:46,741 --> 00:47:49,060
Want me to loan some of
Aunty's jewels for cash?

780
00:47:49,061 --> 00:47:50,621
- No need, Uncle.
- Here you go, Uncle.

781
00:47:55,181 --> 00:47:57,621
- Careful. It's hot.
- Selvi,

782
00:47:58,421 --> 00:48:00,021
Chittu's growing old

783
00:48:00,381 --> 00:48:02,261
and you haven't said anything yet.

784
00:48:02,541 --> 00:48:04,741
Do you expect me
to fall at your feet?

785
00:48:05,301 --> 00:48:07,460
Tell me when
we'll get them married!

786
00:48:07,461 --> 00:48:09,181
Why don't you ask him yourself?

787
00:48:13,901 --> 00:48:15,981
Why the hurry to get her married?

788
00:48:16,461 --> 00:48:17,621
She's still in school.

789
00:48:18,181 --> 00:48:19,861
Plus, there’s a six-year gap
between us.

790
00:48:20,421 --> 00:48:23,380
You know the legal minimum age
for a girl to marry is 18.

791
00:48:23,381 --> 00:48:27,501
Like the folks at our village follow that!

792
00:48:28,141 --> 00:48:29,381
None of your law matters here.

793
00:48:30,021 --> 00:48:31,341
Law, it seems.

794
00:48:32,621 --> 00:48:34,701
There's also a law which allows
widow to remarry.

795
00:48:34,941 --> 00:48:36,901
Does that mean we can get
your mother married again?

796
00:48:41,901 --> 00:48:43,301
Careful, dear.

797
00:48:43,421 --> 00:48:45,061
Help her out, boys.

798
00:48:47,661 --> 00:48:48,981
I'll go.

799
00:48:49,541 --> 00:48:51,660
Hey, you keep Uncle company.

800
00:48:51,661 --> 00:48:52,860
- Wha--
- Vivek?

801
00:48:52,861 --> 00:48:53,901
Come, sit.

802
00:48:55,021 --> 00:48:56,461
He threw me under the bus.

803
00:48:57,141 --> 00:49:00,860
He's a studious idiot.
Ran to the law to escape me.

804
00:49:00,861 --> 00:49:02,021
You tell me, Vivek.

805
00:49:03,301 --> 00:49:04,261
Uncle?

806
00:49:04,821 --> 00:49:06,021
What do you say?

807
00:49:06,581 --> 00:49:07,541
What do I say…

808
00:49:08,181 --> 00:49:11,821
Do you think I'm a fool over here?!

809
00:49:12,981 --> 00:49:14,661
- Selvi? Selvi!
- Huh?

810
00:49:15,141 --> 00:49:16,421
What… What happened?

811
00:49:16,781 --> 00:49:19,341
- I won't put up with this, Selvi.
- Wha…

812
00:49:19,501 --> 00:49:21,381
One of them will be my son-in-law.

813
00:49:21,541 --> 00:49:24,901
- I won't step in until you agree!
- But…

814
00:49:25,061 --> 00:49:26,861
Don't you dare take me for a fool!

815
00:49:27,181 --> 00:49:29,541
- I will end you all!
- Brother…

816
00:49:29,661 --> 00:49:30,821
Please wait!

817
00:49:31,181 --> 00:49:32,621
Let's talk this out!

818
00:49:35,461 --> 00:49:37,380
What did he say?

819
00:49:37,381 --> 00:49:39,101
- Forget about Un--
- You…

820
00:49:39,261 --> 00:49:41,581
Can't believe you're my children!

821
00:49:42,021 --> 00:49:43,301
All my fate!

822
00:49:53,541 --> 00:49:54,741
[phone rings]

823
00:49:55,941 --> 00:49:57,501
Hey, what's happening?

824
00:49:57,941 --> 00:50:00,101
- I'll talk to you later.
- Wait, wait!

825
00:50:00,461 --> 00:50:03,221
Why didn't you call me after
going to Coimbatore.

826
00:50:03,821 --> 00:50:05,501
What happened?
Did you even go?

827
00:50:06,141 --> 00:50:08,421
I did go, but…

828
00:50:08,581 --> 00:50:09,780
Go on, tell me!

829
00:50:09,781 --> 00:50:11,821
- I said I'll talk to you later.
- Vivek…

830
00:50:13,541 --> 00:50:15,580
Vivek, I’m in a tight spot right now!

831
00:50:15,581 --> 00:50:17,420
Tell me what went down there!

832
00:50:17,421 --> 00:50:21,501
Sandhya, I tried my best,
but he's hell-bent on getting her married.

833
00:50:21,941 --> 00:50:23,741
We got into an argument

834
00:50:24,061 --> 00:50:26,061
and even fought a bit.

835
00:50:28,181 --> 00:50:29,220
And then?

836
00:50:29,221 --> 00:50:32,741
His stance and his explanation

837
00:50:33,381 --> 00:50:35,621
slowly made sense to me.

838
00:50:36,221 --> 00:50:37,181
So?

839
00:50:38,781 --> 00:50:39,621
So…

840
00:50:40,381 --> 00:50:42,261
Mom needs to live her life, too.

841
00:50:47,101 --> 00:50:48,541
Why did you two fight?

842
00:50:49,061 --> 00:50:51,700
I mean, I didn't have the strength
to accept it, at first.

843
00:50:51,701 --> 00:50:53,181
Then I decided…

844
00:50:54,581 --> 00:50:56,101
…to side with him.

845
00:51:03,461 --> 00:51:05,461
Hello?
You there, Sandhya?

846
00:51:05,821 --> 00:51:06,861
Vivek…

847
00:51:07,021 --> 00:51:10,340
I'm trying so hard to convince
my parents about us!

848
00:51:10,341 --> 00:51:12,261
I don't even think you realise that.

849
00:51:12,941 --> 00:51:15,940
They're already drilling me
about our caste and status differences,

850
00:51:15,941 --> 00:51:17,780
- and this nonsense to top it all?!
- Sandhya!

851
00:51:17,781 --> 00:51:19,181
Don't dismiss it as nonsense.

852
00:51:19,541 --> 00:51:21,341
My mother's wedding
is equally important.

853
00:51:22,941 --> 00:51:24,300
Vivek…

854
00:51:24,301 --> 00:51:27,821
I wasn't dismissing
or opposing her remarriage.

855
00:51:27,941 --> 00:51:32,101
Which girl's dad will accept
for such conditions?

856
00:51:32,501 --> 00:51:34,500
- Why won't we sort ours--
- Listen to me.

857
00:51:34,501 --> 00:51:36,740
My mother hasn't accepted yet.
It's a long process…

858
00:51:36,741 --> 00:51:38,900
Don't ask me about it
and piss me off!

859
00:51:38,901 --> 00:51:43,141
Sandhya, I don't have an answer
to your hows and whys.

860
00:51:43,341 --> 00:51:45,420
If convincing your parents is our issue,

861
00:51:45,421 --> 00:51:47,341
so is my mother's remarriage.

862
00:51:47,461 --> 00:51:50,061
We've got to figure this out together.

863
00:51:50,901 --> 00:51:53,020
Sandhya? Are you there?

864
00:51:53,021 --> 00:51:54,101
Say something!

865
00:51:55,581 --> 00:51:56,821
Sandhya?

866
00:51:57,741 --> 00:51:59,061
I'm talking to you!

867
00:52:00,101 --> 00:52:01,421
You…

868
00:52:02,901 --> 00:52:04,341
You let me go, Vivek.

869
00:52:06,341 --> 00:52:07,940
I don't think this will work out.

870
00:52:07,941 --> 00:52:10,581
- What?
- I'll get back to studying.

871
00:52:12,741 --> 00:52:14,381
Let's take a break.

872
00:52:14,501 --> 00:52:19,821
You keep escaping by wanting
a break every time we fight!

873
00:52:20,101 --> 00:52:21,301
I wasn't--

874
00:52:22,461 --> 00:52:23,980
I wasn't trying to escape.

875
00:52:23,981 --> 00:52:26,141
- Don't raise your voice at me.
- I wasn't. But make it clear.

876
00:52:26,261 --> 00:52:28,901
Do you want a break from me
or break up with me?

877
00:52:31,461 --> 00:52:32,301
Tell me.

878
00:52:33,101 --> 00:52:35,501
Answer me!
What do you want?!

879
00:52:36,621 --> 00:52:38,901
Do I have to say it?

880
00:52:41,261 --> 00:52:42,501
Let's break up!

881
00:52:42,981 --> 00:52:44,301
Fine, let's break up!

882
00:52:54,701 --> 00:52:55,541
Dang it!

883
00:53:03,781 --> 00:53:04,941
Out of my way.

884
00:53:05,741 --> 00:53:07,221
- This is all your fault.
- What?!

885
00:53:07,341 --> 00:53:08,461
You started it, though!

886
00:53:08,781 --> 00:53:10,621
You asked Sir to ask me, didn't you?

887
00:53:10,981 --> 00:53:13,141
I asked… but when are you replying?

888
00:53:13,981 --> 00:53:16,340
My remarriage would ruin
both your lives.

889
00:53:16,341 --> 00:53:17,781
It won't. We'll be alright.

890
00:53:19,181 --> 00:53:20,780
Oh, really?

891
00:53:20,781 --> 00:53:22,661
Didn't you see him cry?

892
00:53:23,301 --> 00:53:24,901
What was it?
Break up, huh?

893
00:53:25,021 --> 00:53:27,020
Your lives will break up, as well!

894
00:53:27,021 --> 00:53:28,860
- Mom, they'll be al--
- You.

895
00:53:28,861 --> 00:53:31,621
I am not agreeing
even if you two team up!

896
00:53:31,861 --> 00:53:33,301
I won't…

897
00:53:34,061 --> 00:53:35,661
…remarry at this age!

898
00:53:38,301 --> 00:53:41,221
And who do you think you are
to decide my life for me?

899
00:53:49,741 --> 00:53:51,741
[phone rings]

900
00:53:54,421 --> 00:53:56,861
Pick up.
Must be from your girl.

901
00:54:02,981 --> 00:54:04,861
Hi, how are you?

902
00:54:05,221 --> 00:54:08,741
Why didn't you tell us
you were going home?

903
00:54:08,941 --> 00:54:11,741
Had you told us,
I would've sent in a hidden camera.

904
00:54:12,861 --> 00:54:15,621
You could've recorded
your trip for us to use.

905
00:54:15,741 --> 00:54:19,581
It's rare to see a mother and son
having a heart-to-heart, you know?

906
00:54:20,421 --> 00:54:22,181
Also, I heard something.

907
00:54:22,581 --> 00:54:25,780
I felt bad when I found out
you fought with your brother.

908
00:54:25,781 --> 00:54:27,341
That would've been
such amazing content!

909
00:54:27,501 --> 00:54:32,181
Usually, these family vloggers stick to
safe stuff like singing and dancing.

910
00:54:32,341 --> 00:54:33,900
None of them have fought!

911
00:54:33,901 --> 00:54:36,060
Had you recorded it all,

912
00:54:36,061 --> 00:54:38,420
we'd be handed a silver button
for its virality!

913
00:54:38,421 --> 00:54:39,741
- Why don't you--
- You idiot!

914
00:54:39,981 --> 00:54:43,820
Why do you turn everything
into content? It's sickening!

915
00:54:43,821 --> 00:54:45,741
This is our life!
Our personal space!

916
00:54:46,021 --> 00:54:47,421
Do you think it's a content for you?

917
00:54:49,061 --> 00:54:50,220
If you want a silver button,

918
00:54:50,221 --> 00:54:53,101
beg in the streets, record it,
and upload it.

919
00:54:55,061 --> 00:54:56,621
Give the phone to Vandana!

920
00:54:59,221 --> 00:55:00,901
Baskar's on the line.

921
00:55:03,021 --> 00:55:05,301
- Hi!
- Vandana, I'm sorry.

922
00:55:06,021 --> 00:55:07,141
I don't think this will work out.

923
00:55:10,381 --> 00:55:11,581
What won't work out?

924
00:55:11,941 --> 00:55:14,261
My mom isn't…
Hang on, I'll give it to her.

925
00:55:16,861 --> 00:55:18,181
Tell her, Mom.

926
00:55:19,141 --> 00:55:21,021
This is the girl from that channel.

927
00:55:22,101 --> 00:55:24,661
Tell her you're not remarrying
at any cost.

928
00:55:25,541 --> 00:55:26,820
Go on, tell her!

929
00:55:26,821 --> 00:55:28,861
Tell her, just like you told me.

930
00:55:32,981 --> 00:55:34,541
Saw that?

931
00:55:35,261 --> 00:55:36,501
I won’t be getting married either.

932
00:55:37,621 --> 00:55:41,180
We don't have to
put up an act anymore.

933
00:55:41,181 --> 00:55:44,861
We can end our agreement
and the fake drama!

934
00:55:45,021 --> 00:55:45,941
Okay?

935
00:55:46,701 --> 00:55:47,901
I'm sorry.
Bye.

936
00:55:52,141 --> 00:55:54,421
- What’s going on?
- Come on, tell us.

937
00:56:30,661 --> 00:56:32,661
Aren't you two running late?

938
00:56:33,101 --> 00:56:34,021
Come on. Eat your dinner.

939
00:56:37,861 --> 00:56:39,941
Where is he going?
Ask him to eat, first.

940
00:56:40,061 --> 00:56:41,501
- Vivek?
- Mom!

941
00:56:42,021 --> 00:56:43,341
You said we were important.

942
00:56:43,821 --> 00:56:46,541
When we agreed to see you remarry,

943
00:56:47,021 --> 00:56:49,381
- why are you being a coward?
- We'll talk about this later.

944
00:56:49,501 --> 00:56:51,380
Eat up before you leave.

945
00:56:51,381 --> 00:56:52,860
- Vivek?
- You eat it all.

946
00:56:52,861 --> 00:56:55,661
Bas? Bas, wait!
Where will you two eat at this hour?

947
00:56:55,901 --> 00:56:57,661
Don't leave with an empty stomach!

948
00:56:57,781 --> 00:56:58,781
Baskar!

949
00:57:04,461 --> 00:57:07,181
I didn't expect my children

950
00:57:07,301 --> 00:57:09,661
would agree to my remarriage.

951
00:57:10,221 --> 00:57:14,261
I wanted to divert
their attention from this

952
00:57:14,581 --> 00:57:17,140
and decided to scare them…

953
00:57:17,141 --> 00:57:18,661
Yes, sir. I'll work for you.

954
00:57:18,901 --> 00:57:20,901
…by leaving my phone at home
and going to Kerala.

955
00:57:21,181 --> 00:57:23,180
To those who might find out
where I was headed,

956
00:57:23,181 --> 00:57:25,140
We're on a pilgrimage walk
to Maruvathur.

957
00:57:25,141 --> 00:57:28,701
When I saw Mother Mary's procession,
I changed my mind.

958
00:57:29,061 --> 00:57:30,541
But then…

959
00:57:35,421 --> 00:57:37,221
[phone rings]

960
00:57:39,221 --> 00:57:40,101
Brother Baskar?

961
00:57:43,461 --> 00:57:45,821
Shoo!
Go away, you!

962
00:57:47,581 --> 00:57:49,581
Can you check her recent calls?

963
00:57:50,021 --> 00:57:52,100
Last called is a number
saved 'Kerala Sir'.

964
00:57:52,101 --> 00:57:54,181
What, 'Kerala Sir?'

965
00:58:01,301 --> 00:58:03,661
They told me
she was at Melmaruvathur.

966
00:58:03,901 --> 00:58:05,181
Check if she's there!

967
00:59:21,181 --> 00:59:22,101
This is yours, Vivek.

968
00:59:23,701 --> 00:59:25,901
- How's school, Chittu?
- It's going alright.

969
00:59:26,141 --> 00:59:28,620
Mom, hurry!
I'm running late for school!

970
00:59:28,621 --> 00:59:29,861
- I'm coming!
- Bas…

971
00:59:30,021 --> 00:59:32,340
Your mother remembered
to wear my saree to the temple.

972
00:59:32,341 --> 00:59:34,781
But she couldn't inform us
before leaving, huh?

973
00:59:34,941 --> 00:59:37,661
Had she did,
I could've given her my safebox.

974
00:59:44,021 --> 00:59:46,701
All at home have no idea
about her missing

975
00:59:47,581 --> 00:59:50,261
thinking she's gone
to Melmaruvathur.

976
00:59:50,861 --> 00:59:53,341
And you two want
to complain to the police?!

977
00:59:53,781 --> 00:59:55,381
It would be a shame if this got out.

978
00:59:56,221 --> 00:59:57,661
If your mother

979
00:59:57,901 --> 00:59:59,981
intentionally left her phone behind

980
01:00:00,341 --> 01:00:02,501
and went out
without telling either of you,

981
01:00:03,621 --> 01:00:05,261
it suggests

982
01:00:06,061 --> 01:00:08,821
she disapproves
of what you’re up to.

983
01:00:09,341 --> 01:00:10,301
Not again…

984
01:00:11,541 --> 01:00:14,141
It’s probably something

985
01:00:14,941 --> 01:00:17,861
you’re not listening to her about.

986
01:00:19,021 --> 01:00:22,781
I'm certain she wants Chittu
as her daughter-in-law!

987
01:00:23,621 --> 01:00:25,581
Of course, I know my sister!

988
01:00:25,741 --> 01:00:26,941
[phone rings]

989
01:00:33,581 --> 01:00:35,701
What I'm trying to say is…

990
01:00:36,141 --> 01:00:38,141
[phone rings]

991
01:00:40,141 --> 01:00:41,181
Hello?

992
01:00:48,021 --> 01:00:49,620
Yes, Motcham Rani.

993
01:00:49,621 --> 01:00:51,060
You've been with the patient
for three days.

994
01:00:51,061 --> 01:00:52,341
Ma'am.

995
01:00:52,581 --> 01:00:54,301
Where did you see her?

996
01:00:57,261 --> 01:00:59,541
I didn't see her, but heard her.

997
01:00:59,661 --> 01:01:01,460
- You heard her?
- Yes, ma'am.

998
01:01:01,461 --> 01:01:03,820
We were on our way to
Malai Madha Church in a procession

999
01:01:03,821 --> 01:01:05,940
crossing Kallerikuppam when…

1000
01:01:05,941 --> 01:01:08,141
- Lord Ayyanar, save me!
- Oh, no…

1001
01:01:08,661 --> 01:01:11,100
- What's wrong?
- I heard a loud cry.

1002
01:01:11,101 --> 01:01:13,020
- Is it?
- Hurry, hurry!

1003
01:01:13,021 --> 01:01:15,900
- I can't see anyone, Motcham.
- It sounded like a woman!

1004
01:01:15,901 --> 01:01:18,781
I clearly heard them screaming,
"Lord Ayyanar, save me!"

1005
01:01:20,741 --> 01:01:23,381
Don't just stare at the well, Motcham.

1006
01:01:24,021 --> 01:01:25,861
Why would a lady be out
at this hour?

1007
01:01:26,341 --> 01:01:27,980
Don't be stubborn about it.

1008
01:01:27,981 --> 01:01:29,701
Let's get back, people!

1009
01:01:29,941 --> 01:01:31,781
To hell with her scream…

1010
01:01:33,741 --> 01:01:35,381
Let's be on our way, Motcham.

1011
01:01:39,061 --> 01:01:41,101
- Motcham, don't.
- Hey, what are you doing?!

1012
01:01:48,661 --> 01:01:49,541
Hey, come on.

1013
01:01:50,141 --> 01:01:52,701
You don't have to.
Don't cry, dear boy.

1014
01:01:53,141 --> 01:01:55,660
- Please don't cry.
- Doctor, come with me please.

1015
01:01:55,661 --> 01:01:57,981
Motcham, come with me.
You too, boys.

1016
01:01:58,581 --> 01:01:59,540
Come with me.

1017
01:01:59,541 --> 01:02:01,580
When will we get her final report?

1018
01:02:01,581 --> 01:02:03,261
As soon as the MRI results are in.

1019
01:02:03,541 --> 01:02:05,780
All of you must sign.
Even you, boys.

1020
01:02:05,781 --> 01:02:07,301
Sure, ma'am.

1021
01:02:08,021 --> 01:02:09,421
They've come out.
You can go in, boys.

1022
01:02:10,541 --> 01:02:12,261
She says a hog butt her into the well.

1023
01:02:12,941 --> 01:02:15,781
I asked her why she left without
telling us.

1024
01:02:15,981 --> 01:02:17,020
But she never said a word.

1025
01:02:17,021 --> 01:02:19,101
She kept mum about it.

1026
01:02:20,301 --> 01:02:23,740
What really happened, Bas?
Do you know anything?

1027
01:02:23,741 --> 01:02:25,261
Tell us if you do.

1028
01:02:28,181 --> 01:02:29,581
Okay, that's enough.

1029
01:02:29,701 --> 01:02:31,220
She was in a coma for a day, right?

1030
01:02:31,221 --> 01:02:32,501
It must be hard
to remember things at once.

1031
01:02:32,741 --> 01:02:36,020
Baskar, take him with you
and visit your mother.

1032
01:02:36,021 --> 01:02:38,501
Wa-- Wait a minute
I've got something to tell her.

1033
01:02:40,181 --> 01:02:41,981
See how he runs to her
before her own kids.

1034
01:02:57,021 --> 01:02:58,341
My children…

1035
01:02:58,461 --> 01:02:59,661
Don't strain yourself to talk.

1036
01:03:00,221 --> 01:03:01,421
I'll figure it out.

1037
01:03:02,661 --> 01:03:06,380
I understand how you must feel
with Vivek and Baskar

1038
01:03:06,381 --> 01:03:08,501
unwilling to step forward
to marry Chittu.

1039
01:03:09,821 --> 01:03:12,141
But you jumping into the well
was stupid!

1040
01:03:13,261 --> 01:03:16,461
I mean, it did work out

1041
01:03:17,061 --> 01:03:19,501
because your boys
are scared to bits!

1042
01:03:20,621 --> 01:03:21,861
I'll send them in now.

1043
01:03:22,141 --> 01:03:24,621
Brainwash either of them
to be my son-in-law, okay?

1044
01:03:26,661 --> 01:03:27,741
I'll see you.

1045
01:03:28,381 --> 01:03:29,541
Ugh…

1046
01:03:36,781 --> 01:03:38,861
The moment I hit my head,
all I could think was…

1047
01:03:38,981 --> 01:03:42,821
will I ever see my children again?

1048
01:03:43,741 --> 01:03:45,061
I shouldn't have…

1049
01:03:45,421 --> 01:03:47,501
put my babies through so much.

1050
01:03:59,421 --> 01:04:00,621
Sorry, Mom.

1051
01:04:01,981 --> 01:04:03,301
Forgive me, Mom.

1052
01:04:05,461 --> 01:04:08,261
I should've apologised.
But didn't.

1053
01:04:08,501 --> 01:04:12,061
Because if I did,
they'd bring up my remarriage.

1054
01:04:12,541 --> 01:04:14,021
So, I remained quiet.

1055
01:04:34,701 --> 01:04:36,981
You wrapped everything up, yeah?

1056
01:04:38,141 --> 01:04:39,221
Not like I had a choice.

1057
01:04:39,421 --> 01:04:42,061
Her life's more important
than her remarriage.

1058
01:04:43,501 --> 01:04:44,781
Have they discharged her?

1059
01:04:45,541 --> 01:04:47,340
Yeah. Vivek's with her.

1060
01:04:47,341 --> 01:04:48,741
- Coffee?
- Black.

1061
01:05:15,221 --> 01:05:16,221
Hey.

1062
01:05:16,701 --> 01:05:19,501
Hey, Baskar?!
What's wrong?

1063
01:05:19,821 --> 01:05:22,181
Baskar?
What happened?!

1064
01:05:22,861 --> 01:05:24,941
Baskar!
What's wrong?

1065
01:05:26,221 --> 01:05:27,301
Why're you crying?

1066
01:05:32,621 --> 01:05:33,701
Mom…

1067
01:05:34,341 --> 01:05:35,981
Mom will be all alone

1068
01:05:36,101 --> 01:05:39,181
drinking black coffee by herself.

1069
01:05:50,021 --> 01:05:54,980
♪ From far clouds comes a gentle tear
Which root it finds is never clear ♪

1070
01:05:54,981 --> 01:05:58,341
♪ No one’s seen it anywhere here ♪

1071
01:05:59,701 --> 01:06:04,620
♪ Wind hits bamboo all along
When does it change into a song? ♪

1072
01:06:04,621 --> 01:06:08,181
♪ No one’s known it all this long ♪

1073
01:06:08,981 --> 01:06:11,340
♪ My heart’s restless, it slips away ♪

1074
01:06:11,341 --> 01:06:13,580
♪ It runs to you, won’t ever stay ♪

1075
01:06:13,581 --> 01:06:15,980
♪ I tried, I held ♪

1076
01:06:15,981 --> 01:06:18,581
♪ But I fell through ♪

1077
01:06:19,061 --> 01:06:23,541
♪ Dreams are falling like a stream
Filling up my eyes with gleam ♪

1078
01:06:23,901 --> 01:06:28,181
♪ I beckoned you with my touch ♪

1079
01:06:30,701 --> 01:06:32,300
You like him?!

1080
01:06:32,301 --> 01:06:33,781
You wretch.

1081
01:06:33,941 --> 01:06:37,180
We let you be for a night
and this is what you do to the house?!

1082
01:06:37,181 --> 01:06:39,380
- You vermin!
- Of course, I'd do this!

1083
01:06:39,381 --> 01:06:41,940
- As if Dad's actions were justifiable.
- So?

1084
01:06:41,941 --> 01:06:44,900
- You want to accept your nonsense?
- Punish me then!

1085
01:06:44,901 --> 01:06:48,101
Instead, you vandalized their walls.
How is it fair?

1086
01:06:48,261 --> 01:06:51,141
He never once spoke ill of you!

1087
01:06:51,341 --> 01:06:53,500
So this was your revenge?

1088
01:06:53,501 --> 01:06:55,300
- Sir?
- Check who's by the door.

1089
01:06:55,301 --> 01:06:56,221
Senthil sir?

1090
01:06:56,901 --> 01:06:59,661
God, ugh! I paid for
all those art classes for this?!

1091
01:06:59,781 --> 01:07:01,420
- I curse you!
- Stop hitting me!

1092
01:07:01,421 --> 01:07:03,300
I asked you to bring people over
to scrub that off.

1093
01:07:03,301 --> 01:07:05,420
They're here and on it, already!

1094
01:07:05,421 --> 01:07:07,061
Paint over that crap, man.

1095
01:07:11,181 --> 01:07:14,701
Make it quick
before someone knows.

1096
01:07:16,541 --> 01:07:18,021
- Driver?
- Yeah.

1097
01:07:18,221 --> 01:07:22,661
I wonder how she climbed up
those high walls and painted this!

1098
01:07:22,821 --> 01:07:24,261
It's confusing!

1099
01:07:25,421 --> 01:07:27,061
That's love.

1100
01:07:27,421 --> 01:07:28,900
You'll never know.

1101
01:07:28,901 --> 01:07:30,541
- Me?
- Yeah.

1102
01:07:31,781 --> 01:07:35,061
♪ Touch me slow,
I was bare ground ♪

1103
01:07:35,421 --> 01:07:36,500
FEW MONTHS LATER

1104
01:07:36,501 --> 01:07:37,621
Here, man.

1105
01:07:38,101 --> 01:07:39,541
Fetch me some water, buddy.

1106
01:07:41,221 --> 01:07:43,101
Here, Shankar.

1107
01:07:49,821 --> 01:07:51,821
Hurry, hurry!

1108
01:08:08,901 --> 01:08:10,541
Drink a little, dear.

1109
01:08:22,621 --> 01:08:23,941
This moron…

1110
01:08:25,261 --> 01:08:26,101
Here you go.

1111
01:08:32,300 --> 01:08:33,581
Dang it, he's smart.

1112
01:08:34,300 --> 01:08:37,300
No!
My precious boy's here!

1113
01:08:37,581 --> 01:08:39,621
My poor baby!

1114
01:08:42,061 --> 01:08:43,541
Dear!

1115
01:08:44,661 --> 01:08:45,940
Don't scream loudly, dear.

1116
01:08:45,941 --> 01:08:47,941
She's going into labor, oh God!

1117
01:08:48,181 --> 01:08:51,420
- Water! Someone fetch some water!
- Move! Move!

1118
01:08:54,300 --> 01:08:56,741
Careful, Selvi!
Two lives are at risk!

1119
01:08:57,701 --> 01:08:58,981
Baskar!

1120
01:08:59,460 --> 01:09:01,101
Baskar, bring the stretcher over.

1121
01:09:01,541 --> 01:09:03,300
- Get here quick!
- Lift up! Lift up!

1122
01:09:04,141 --> 01:09:06,180
Move! Move!
Move, please!

1123
01:09:06,181 --> 01:09:08,260
Lay her down
on the stretcher.

1124
01:09:08,261 --> 01:09:10,621
Be careful of her legs.

1125
01:09:13,581 --> 01:09:15,581
Oh, God!

1126
01:09:15,861 --> 01:09:18,380
Dear!

1127
01:09:19,061 --> 01:09:21,261
- My dear!
- Baskar?

1128
01:09:21,460 --> 01:09:24,300
Don't stall and take her quickly!

1129
01:09:24,941 --> 01:09:27,541
Be quick! She's in grave danger!

1130
01:09:34,541 --> 01:09:37,300
Follow us on your bike, Baskar.

1131
01:09:37,661 --> 01:09:39,661
Go! Go! All will be fine!

1132
01:09:40,300 --> 01:09:41,701
Hey, come on! Get the bike!

1133
01:09:58,501 --> 01:10:00,501
Selvi, come eat.

1134
01:10:12,941 --> 01:10:14,740
It's getting late.
Let's go.

1135
01:10:14,741 --> 01:10:15,940
Let me rush to the bathroom quick.

1136
01:10:15,941 --> 01:10:18,181
Great timing.
Hurry up and don't delay!

1137
01:10:32,461 --> 01:10:35,181
Now why are you
putting on an act by crying?

1138
01:10:35,621 --> 01:10:37,781
You've been crying like you know them!

1139
01:10:37,941 --> 01:10:39,981
Who do you think you are?
Sivaji or Savithri?!

1140
01:10:41,861 --> 01:10:45,020
How dare you call me that?
I'm putting on a show, huh?!

1141
01:10:45,021 --> 01:10:47,901
Well, tell me!
Am I a drama queen?

1142
01:10:50,181 --> 01:10:52,421
I knew Megala as a child

1143
01:10:52,821 --> 01:10:54,501
who now has a child of her own!

1144
01:10:55,861 --> 01:10:59,981
I was 26
when I lost my husband.

1145
01:11:02,181 --> 01:11:05,101
But she? She's barely 20.

1146
01:11:07,181 --> 01:11:12,781
From now on, she won’t feel safe
around anyone in this village.

1147
01:11:13,821 --> 01:11:17,141
Her life's already over
even before it could begin!

1148
01:11:18,581 --> 01:11:19,621
The end.

1149
01:11:20,101 --> 01:11:22,261
Damn this life!

1150
01:11:23,221 --> 01:11:26,421
You know what this feels like, right?

1151
01:11:27,061 --> 01:11:29,141
Can’t you try to change it?

1152
01:11:29,901 --> 01:11:33,461
Start small at least
to create a ripple of change!

1153
01:11:33,781 --> 01:11:35,740
Of course, it'll be difficult

1154
01:11:35,741 --> 01:11:37,221
with many opposing
and causing trouble.

1155
01:11:37,461 --> 01:11:41,141
But the tears that come
once you get past it, is the real deal.

1156
01:11:41,381 --> 01:11:42,981
And what you did now,
is just an act.

1157
01:11:43,781 --> 01:11:45,341
If you want Megala's life

1158
01:11:45,781 --> 01:11:48,300
and the lives of women seperated
from their husbands to get better,

1159
01:11:48,301 --> 01:11:50,981
- you make the first move.
- Baskar, that’s enough.

1160
01:11:51,101 --> 01:11:52,221
Move.

1161
01:11:52,621 --> 01:11:54,820
Only when you remarry at 43,

1162
01:11:54,821 --> 01:11:58,621
will our 23 year old Megala
and other Megalas will get a better life!

1163
01:11:59,941 --> 01:12:04,781
Until then, your crying
and whining is all a show!

1164
01:12:05,221 --> 01:12:07,021
You're Sivaji and Savithri!

1165
01:12:07,581 --> 01:12:08,541
I'm done with you.

1166
01:12:21,541 --> 01:12:22,621
Selvi?

1167
01:12:24,021 --> 01:12:25,141
Are you coming or not?

1168
01:12:35,581 --> 01:12:40,101
♪ A woman's heart is an endless sea ♪

1169
01:12:40,261 --> 01:12:45,261
[phone ringing]
♪ No shore can hold its mystery ♪

1170
01:12:47,221 --> 01:12:48,661
Driver, can you turn
the volume down a bit?

1171
01:12:50,901 --> 01:12:51,941
Mom?

1172
01:12:55,181 --> 01:12:56,141
Mom?

1173
01:13:01,141 --> 01:13:02,221
Mom!

1174
01:13:04,061 --> 01:13:05,261
Go ahead.

1175
01:13:08,581 --> 01:13:09,501
Mom…

1176
01:13:10,101 --> 01:13:11,141
Proceed with it.

1177
01:13:12,541 --> 01:13:13,821
We'll face, come what may.

1178
01:13:17,181 --> 01:13:18,541
We'll go ahead, Mom.

1179
01:13:19,941 --> 01:13:20,901
We'll proceed.

1180
01:13:21,941 --> 01:13:23,101
We'll proceed!

1181
01:13:23,781 --> 01:13:24,661
Let's go ahead!

1182
01:13:25,541 --> 01:13:26,421
Let's go ahead!

1183
01:13:39,421 --> 01:13:42,980
♪ Hey yo, hey yo
Where’s your guy, yo? ♪

1184
01:13:42,981 --> 01:13:46,380
♪ Who is he? Who could it be?
Who’s your man, tell me! ♪

1185
01:13:46,381 --> 01:13:49,941
♪ Hey yo, hey yo,
Wedding bells say hey yo! ♪

1186
01:13:50,821 --> 01:13:53,780
We'll deal with this privately
till my Mom finds a partner.

1187
01:13:53,781 --> 01:13:55,900
♪ Hey yo, hey yo
Leaves and trees all say so! ♪

1188
01:13:55,901 --> 01:13:58,021
You might have to move with me
to Kuwait after the wedding.

1189
01:13:59,861 --> 01:14:03,940
Find someone who lives
within overnight reach of me.

1190
01:14:03,941 --> 01:14:05,461
To hell with Kuwait, Muscat…

1191
01:14:06,781 --> 01:14:10,141
♪ Who is he? Who could it be?
Where is he? ♪

1192
01:14:23,781 --> 01:14:26,940
♪ One by one, it’s falling in
Run and chase it, let’s begin ♪

1193
01:14:26,941 --> 01:14:28,461
So what if he's a priest?

1194
01:14:28,581 --> 01:14:29,661
No, no.

1195
01:14:29,861 --> 01:14:31,700
We read that you're a priest.

1196
01:14:31,701 --> 01:14:33,861
- At which temple?
- Yep, I am a priest.

1197
01:14:34,101 --> 01:14:35,781
My temple…

1198
01:14:36,541 --> 01:14:37,501
Look over there!

1199
01:14:38,141 --> 01:14:40,981
Sairam! Sairam!

1200
01:14:41,181 --> 01:14:42,941
Sairam! Sairam!

1201
01:14:44,341 --> 01:14:47,740
♪ Family lines up, gifts to give
Gold in hand; let’s start to live! ♪

1202
01:14:47,741 --> 01:14:51,340
♪ Tie his heart and make him stay
First night shows the way ♪

1203
01:14:51,341 --> 01:14:54,061
♪ Still a world you’ve yet to see
In the dark, just you and he ♪

1204
01:15:08,141 --> 01:15:11,700
♪ Hey yo, hey yo
Where’s your guy, yo? ♪

1205
01:15:11,701 --> 01:15:15,021
♪ Who is he? Who could it be?
Who’s your man, tell me! ♪

1206
01:15:15,141 --> 01:15:18,500
♪ Hundreds of joys, sweet as can be
Honey-like love flowing free ♪

1207
01:15:18,501 --> 01:15:21,980
♪ Love and desire, both in play
Who can keep them both away? ♪

1208
01:15:21,981 --> 01:15:25,221
♪ Hey yo, hey yo,
Wedding bells say hey yo! ♪

1209
01:15:25,341 --> 01:15:28,780
♪ Even if sleep drifts far away
It still feels like a concert play ♪

1210
01:15:28,781 --> 01:15:32,180
♪ Hey yo, hey yo
Where’s your guy, yo? ♪

1211
01:15:32,181 --> 01:15:35,060
♪ The dream I kept within my sight
He’ll give it to me-- ♪

1212
01:15:35,061 --> 01:15:36,661
How many tickets did that lady buy?

1213
01:15:36,901 --> 01:15:38,421
Did she offer to buy for the broker?

1214
01:15:38,661 --> 01:15:40,461
First, buy your ticket!

1215
01:15:40,661 --> 01:15:42,701
Tickets, tickets…
To where, ma'am?

1216
01:15:43,301 --> 01:15:44,221
Got spare change?

1217
01:15:46,301 --> 01:15:48,661
FEW MONTHS LATER

1218
01:15:57,901 --> 01:16:01,461
Mother Mary, their pilgrimage was ruined
last year because of my accident.

1219
01:16:01,901 --> 01:16:05,821
I humbly pray that
you grant Motcham’s wish.

1220
01:16:06,101 --> 01:16:10,261
Mother Mary, let my wish
be fulfilled this year.

1221
01:16:10,421 --> 01:16:14,181
Please help us find
a bride for Ezhumalai!

1222
01:16:22,381 --> 01:16:23,540
Getting hungry?

1223
01:16:23,541 --> 01:16:25,381
- Hang on, I'll untie you--
- Motcham?

1224
01:16:26,381 --> 01:16:28,021
Hey, come on in!

1225
01:16:28,381 --> 01:16:30,860
- Dear?
- Every morning you pester me!

1226
01:16:30,861 --> 01:16:31,941
Selvi's here.

1227
01:16:32,221 --> 01:16:34,340
- Welcome. Come on in.
- Where's Brother?

1228
01:16:34,341 --> 01:16:36,461
Must be out fetching water.
Wait, I'll call him here.

1229
01:16:36,621 --> 01:16:38,660
Someone said they'll come
in the afternoon.

1230
01:16:38,661 --> 01:16:40,140
What made you come early?

1231
01:16:40,141 --> 01:16:42,541
Motcham, both of you
come to Ezhumalai's house.

1232
01:16:42,741 --> 01:16:44,300
Come, let's be on our way.

1233
01:16:44,301 --> 01:16:46,940
- I thought I'd spend some time in--
- As if!

1234
01:16:46,941 --> 01:16:49,821
Like that's the reason
you got here early.

1235
01:16:52,701 --> 01:16:54,980
I'll be back
to take you grazing, okay?

1236
01:16:54,981 --> 01:16:58,181
I’m taking my girl
to meet her man.

1237
01:17:00,661 --> 01:17:03,661
I know you told your cow
I'm your girl.

1238
01:17:03,941 --> 01:17:06,260
But I'll decide if he's my man!

1239
01:17:06,261 --> 01:17:09,101
Take your sweet time.
No one's rushing.

1240
01:17:10,621 --> 01:17:12,020
- We're here.
- Hi, Motcham!

1241
01:17:12,021 --> 01:17:14,060
Is she a guest?
What's the occasion?

1242
01:17:14,061 --> 01:17:15,780
I mean, it is an occasion.

1243
01:17:15,781 --> 01:17:17,981
- I'll tell you later.
- Alright, be well.

1244
01:17:19,381 --> 01:17:20,941
- Granny?
- Who's asking?

1245
01:17:21,381 --> 01:17:22,580
Come in!

1246
01:17:22,581 --> 01:17:24,421
- Granny?
- Yeah?

1247
01:17:25,341 --> 01:17:27,020
Don't just stand here. Come close!

1248
01:17:27,021 --> 01:17:27,980
Don't be afraid.

1249
01:17:27,981 --> 01:17:29,980
I saved you from the deepest well,

1250
01:17:29,981 --> 01:17:31,780
but he's just got a pumpset.

1251
01:17:31,781 --> 01:17:32,821
Come on in.

1252
01:17:32,941 --> 01:17:34,181
Hello, Granny.

1253
01:17:34,421 --> 01:17:36,340
- Oh, is this Motcham?
- Yes, yes.

1254
01:17:36,341 --> 01:17:38,021
- Who's with you?
- She's um…

1255
01:17:38,541 --> 01:17:39,740
- I'll tell you.
- Okay.

1256
01:17:39,741 --> 01:17:41,221
Hey, go look around.

1257
01:17:41,541 --> 01:17:43,821
- Off you go.
- Go, dear.

1258
01:17:46,381 --> 01:17:50,181
Granny, she is Ezhumalai's…

1259
01:18:18,061 --> 01:18:20,141
Welcome! Welcome!

1260
01:18:20,501 --> 01:18:23,461
Thought I'd fetch some water
before bringing the curry to a boil.

1261
01:18:23,701 --> 01:18:26,141
Arokia just told me
about your visit.

1262
01:18:27,141 --> 01:18:28,661
Gosh, the sun's really blistering!

1263
01:18:29,021 --> 01:18:31,541
I wonder how you walked in this heat.
I couldn't--

1264
01:18:41,181 --> 01:18:43,261
Careful!
You might burn yourself.

1265
01:18:43,621 --> 01:18:44,740
Go on.

1266
01:18:44,741 --> 01:18:45,941
You can try it out.

1267
01:18:46,101 --> 01:18:47,300
Please.

1268
01:18:47,301 --> 01:18:48,581
Don't expect it to be great.

1269
01:18:52,021 --> 01:18:53,741
Also, don’t be surprised to see
so many kitchen appliances here.

1270
01:18:54,861 --> 01:18:57,141
I bought this for my wife
when she was alive.

1271
01:18:57,661 --> 01:19:01,061
I know pretty accessories
make them happy.

1272
01:19:01,421 --> 01:19:04,381
But I felt the best thing I could do
was buy her kitchen appliances

1273
01:19:04,901 --> 01:19:06,261
to make her life easier.

1274
01:19:08,141 --> 01:19:10,821
Ezhumalai, I'm leaving.
Got to take the cows grazing.

1275
01:19:10,941 --> 01:19:13,660
Brother, can you drop Selvi
by the riverside?

1276
01:19:13,661 --> 01:19:14,700
- She'll go from there.
- Alright.

1277
01:19:14,701 --> 01:19:16,380
- Bye, Selvi!
- No, I--

1278
01:19:16,381 --> 01:19:18,701
Hey, I can drop you off.
Don't worry. Give me a minute.

1279
01:19:22,741 --> 01:19:24,621
I was 19 when I went to Oman.

1280
01:19:25,461 --> 01:19:26,581
I was farming there, too.

1281
01:19:27,261 --> 01:19:28,381
Date palms!

1282
01:19:28,981 --> 01:19:30,741
Twenty years went just like that
in a desert.

1283
01:19:31,261 --> 01:19:33,821
You know,
Oman's an Arab country.

1284
01:19:34,421 --> 01:19:37,021
I know.
Muscat is its airport, right?

1285
01:19:37,301 --> 01:19:39,221
My, my!
How do you know that?

1286
01:19:39,701 --> 01:19:41,900
I was working in a travel agency.

1287
01:19:41,901 --> 01:19:43,501
Riyal is it's currency, right?

1288
01:19:43,741 --> 01:19:45,260
I have a keepsake of it.

1289
01:19:45,261 --> 01:19:47,381
Ah, I too have one!

1290
01:19:47,501 --> 01:19:48,541
Come over here.

1291
01:19:50,301 --> 01:19:51,221
See this?

1292
01:19:53,981 --> 01:19:55,141
Take a closer look!

1293
01:19:57,381 --> 01:19:59,261
Recognise the 'sheikh?'

1294
01:20:02,861 --> 01:20:03,821
Yep, that's me!

1295
01:20:07,501 --> 01:20:09,301
It's alright, you can laugh at it!

1296
01:20:10,301 --> 01:20:12,340
Why…
Why have you stuck that there?

1297
01:20:12,341 --> 01:20:15,381
I owe my life to Oman.

1298
01:20:15,501 --> 01:20:18,741
Despite its barren dunes,
you must remain grateful.

1299
01:20:19,101 --> 01:20:20,101
Come along.

1300
01:20:20,941 --> 01:20:24,061
I think I went home only four times.

1301
01:20:24,421 --> 01:20:25,621
Ah, popsicles!
Sir…

1302
01:20:26,141 --> 01:20:27,061
Two, please.

1303
01:20:27,541 --> 01:20:29,900
- I… don't want.
- Have a bite!

1304
01:20:29,901 --> 01:20:31,621
- It's… alright.
- Ah, eat one to beat the heat.

1305
01:20:31,821 --> 01:20:33,541
- No, I really don't want.
- Oh, yeah?

1306
01:20:36,741 --> 01:20:38,181
Alright then.

1307
01:20:43,381 --> 01:20:46,941
Only after, Sembaruthi, my daughter
got married did she realise

1308
01:20:47,101 --> 01:20:50,781
that I also remarry,
so I won't be alone.

1309
01:20:54,021 --> 01:20:55,461
How sloppy can I be!

1310
01:20:58,341 --> 01:20:59,661
You're laughing for this, too?

1311
01:21:02,421 --> 01:21:06,060
Do you want me to be happy
that I'm with you

1312
01:21:06,061 --> 01:21:08,701
or sad because
I let my icecream melt?

1313
01:21:09,741 --> 01:21:13,180
It's only ice. It melts even if it falls
on sand or in my mouth.

1314
01:21:13,181 --> 01:21:15,820
It's taking its course.
And we'll take ours!

1315
01:21:15,821 --> 01:21:17,700
What do you mean by ours?

1316
01:21:17,701 --> 01:21:19,781
Ours is… staying happy!

1317
01:21:21,621 --> 01:21:23,221
Looking on the bright side feels nice.

1318
01:21:23,421 --> 01:21:25,741
But keeping that hope alive is tough.

1319
01:21:26,421 --> 01:21:28,821
Why not?
You have me, now.

1320
01:21:28,941 --> 01:21:31,420
All this anger and sorrow in us
must remain in us.

1321
01:21:31,421 --> 01:21:32,861
We mustn't be slaves to it.

1322
01:21:33,741 --> 01:21:36,301
You must know that
happy people aren't fools.

1323
01:21:36,701 --> 01:21:39,861
Your friend, Motcham,
asked me to drop you by the river.

1324
01:21:40,141 --> 01:21:41,541
And I took my bike out.

1325
01:21:41,821 --> 01:21:43,381
But did I actually drop you?

1326
01:21:44,901 --> 01:21:46,341
Does that make me a fool?

1327
01:21:48,181 --> 01:21:50,981
Fine, tell me why you're happy?

1328
01:21:52,541 --> 01:21:54,821
Because I really, really like you!

1329
01:21:56,821 --> 01:21:57,861
Why?

1330
01:21:57,981 --> 01:22:01,061
Ask this when someone
doesn't like you.

1331
01:22:01,741 --> 01:22:03,941
How are you so clueless?

1332
01:22:06,941 --> 01:22:09,180
Let me… take the bike from here on.

1333
01:22:09,181 --> 01:22:10,381
You can walk along.

1334
01:22:11,661 --> 01:22:13,061
Why do you seem quiet?

1335
01:22:14,221 --> 01:22:15,141
No, I…

1336
01:22:15,701 --> 01:22:18,301
I'm not able to be happy like you.

1337
01:22:18,501 --> 01:22:20,581
Eh? Why not?

1338
01:22:22,581 --> 01:22:25,381
Not sure what my kids think…

1339
01:22:26,141 --> 01:22:28,341
You can think about that afterwards.

1340
01:22:29,021 --> 01:22:30,901
Let's start with
you doing the things you like.

1341
01:22:31,381 --> 01:22:34,181
And when they start liking me,
you can be even happier!

1342
01:22:36,581 --> 01:22:39,260
See, we must never waste a day.

1343
01:22:39,261 --> 01:22:40,661
We're in our 40s!

1344
01:22:40,821 --> 01:22:42,901
In our 20s, a day might count as a day.

1345
01:22:43,021 --> 01:22:45,621
As we grow into our 40s,
a day feels like a year!

1346
01:22:47,701 --> 01:22:48,621
Also,

1347
01:22:49,301 --> 01:22:51,301
I remembered something
when you mentioned about your kids.

1348
01:22:51,861 --> 01:22:52,861
The person you met at home,

1349
01:22:53,661 --> 01:22:54,781
is my aunt.

1350
01:22:55,581 --> 01:22:57,261
She is paralyzed.

1351
01:22:57,541 --> 01:23:01,861
So, she eats, sleeps,
goes to the loo…

1352
01:23:02,701 --> 01:23:04,101
…all on the bed.

1353
01:23:05,021 --> 01:23:07,940
She'll remain my responsibility
even after our wedding.

1354
01:23:07,941 --> 01:23:11,581
She's not your responsibilty.
Make sure your sons know about this.

1355
01:23:23,141 --> 01:23:24,460
Hey…

1356
01:23:24,461 --> 01:23:26,821
You're walking away
without a word?

1357
01:23:35,901 --> 01:23:38,981
If I’m to be anything,
I want to be like you.

1358
01:23:39,821 --> 01:23:43,021
All I feel is
the need to be with you.

1359
01:23:43,621 --> 01:23:50,581
♪ Talking with you, I began to fly
Carried in a dreamy sky ♪

1360
01:23:53,901 --> 01:24:00,581
♪ Walking ahead, I slowly fell
Like a tender rain that softly fell ♪

1361
01:24:02,461 --> 01:24:06,060
♪ My heart runs wild
With endless waves ♪

1362
01:24:06,061 --> 01:24:08,620
♪ A gentle rain that softly stays ♪

1363
01:24:08,621 --> 01:24:12,780
♪ I melt away in love’s own blaze ♪

1364
01:24:12,781 --> 01:24:16,220
♪ I wandered long to find my own ♪

1365
01:24:16,221 --> 01:24:19,100
♪ Days kept fading, I was alone ♪

1366
01:24:19,101 --> 01:24:23,020
♪ And today, I found you ♪

1367
01:24:23,021 --> 01:24:27,901
♪ No one was mine till this day ♪

1368
01:24:28,101 --> 01:24:33,141
♪ Now it’s us, come what may ♪

1369
01:24:33,261 --> 01:24:38,300
♪ A net of memories drifting free ♪

1370
01:24:38,301 --> 01:24:44,021
♪ Eyes that speak but lose to me ♪

1371
01:24:48,061 --> 01:24:49,381
I like him.

1372
01:24:50,421 --> 01:24:52,741
Baskar and Vivek will like him, right?

1373
01:24:54,181 --> 01:24:55,901
Tell me!

1374
01:24:56,341 --> 01:24:57,541
Tell me that they will.

1375
01:24:58,741 --> 01:25:00,181
Like you can answer me any way.

1376
01:25:08,141 --> 01:25:12,461
♪ A dream that feels unreal ♪

1377
01:25:13,301 --> 01:25:17,941
♪ Or a memory I can’t hold still?
I’m lost and still ♪

1378
01:25:18,181 --> 01:25:21,741
- I like him.
- ♪ A moon that draws so close to me ♪

1379
01:25:23,181 --> 01:25:28,141
♪ Something only my heart knows?
I’m lost in its flow ♪

1380
01:25:28,421 --> 01:25:31,981
♪ Thinking of you! ♪

1381
01:25:41,661 --> 01:25:43,540
- Do you have a picture of her?
- No, dear.

1382
01:25:43,541 --> 01:25:44,821
You really don't?

1383
01:25:45,781 --> 01:25:46,781
Dad?

1384
01:25:47,301 --> 01:25:48,821
Got it from Motcham Sister.

1385
01:25:49,501 --> 01:25:50,501
Alright, dear.

1386
01:26:00,741 --> 01:26:04,741
♪ Is this a love that never fades? ♪

1387
01:26:05,221 --> 01:26:08,460
♪ What is this tie we’ve drawn upon? ♪

1388
01:26:08,461 --> 01:26:10,861
♪ A bond that time has carried on ♪

1389
01:26:10,981 --> 01:26:15,260
♪ Is this a search that never ends? ♪

1390
01:26:15,261 --> 01:26:18,740
♪ My heart crosses every distance ♪

1391
01:26:18,741 --> 01:26:21,100
♪ Pleading with quiet pain ♪

1392
01:26:21,101 --> 01:26:23,700
♪ Feels like a dream
I can’t quite see ♪

1393
01:26:23,701 --> 01:26:26,340
♪ Still my hands reach out
To you and me ♪

1394
01:26:26,341 --> 01:26:28,541
♪ You’re you, I’m me, worlds apart ♪

1395
01:26:28,701 --> 01:26:31,300
♪ Yet many roads can meet our hearts ♪

1396
01:26:31,301 --> 01:26:33,900
♪ So many longings fill me inside ♪

1397
01:26:33,901 --> 01:26:36,500
♪ Searching for you
We slowly collide ♪

1398
01:26:36,501 --> 01:26:40,180
♪ In the silence of words we hide
Desire comes rushing inside ♪

1399
01:26:40,181 --> 01:26:44,941
♪ The time will come
We’ll fall into place ♪

1400
01:26:45,061 --> 01:26:49,781
♪ The moment will run
For our hands to embrace ♪

1401
01:26:50,061 --> 01:26:54,781
♪ All our doubts will slip away ♪

1402
01:26:55,301 --> 01:27:00,141
♪ Every barrier will change one day ♪

1403
01:27:03,221 --> 01:27:06,701
♪ A dream that feels unreal ♪

1404
01:27:08,221 --> 01:27:13,221
♪ Or a memory I can’t hold still?
I’m lost and still ♪

1405
01:27:13,541 --> 01:27:17,381
♪ A moon that draws so close to me ♪

1406
01:27:18,221 --> 01:27:23,740
♪ Something only my heart knows?
I’m lost in its flow ♪

1407
01:27:23,741 --> 01:27:28,141
♪ Thinking of you! ♪

1408
01:27:44,141 --> 01:27:47,501
♪ A dream that feels unreal ♪

1409
01:27:49,461 --> 01:27:51,500
Which one of them is the--

1410
01:27:51,501 --> 01:27:52,661
Ezhumalai?

1411
01:27:53,181 --> 01:27:54,381
- This is her son.
- Hello.

1412
01:27:59,461 --> 01:28:00,940
I swear, Ezhumalai.

1413
01:28:00,941 --> 01:28:02,340
- Don't bother about him.
- Baskar?

1414
01:28:02,341 --> 01:28:05,381
Since today's an auspicious day,
we thought we'd fix their wedding date.

1415
01:28:05,661 --> 01:28:06,620
Give that to me.

1416
01:28:06,621 --> 01:28:08,861
Whoa. Hold up.
Hang on a minute.

1417
01:28:09,061 --> 01:28:11,101
Why don't we take this slow?

1418
01:28:12,141 --> 01:28:14,461
- Because…
- What's wrong?

1419
01:28:15,021 --> 01:28:17,941
Since this is the first time here,

1420
01:28:18,421 --> 01:28:20,141
we'll visit your place, tomorrow.

1421
01:28:21,781 --> 01:28:23,461
Also, we need Vivek's approval.

1422
01:28:24,501 --> 01:28:25,301
Let's see…

1423
01:28:25,741 --> 01:28:27,181
if everything falls in place.

1424
01:28:28,701 --> 01:28:31,861
When it does, we'll fix the date
on an auspicious day!

1425
01:28:42,061 --> 01:28:44,341
Alright, dear. Alright.

1426
01:28:47,461 --> 01:28:49,461
Mom, I'm stopping by
at Manohar's place.

1427
01:29:01,341 --> 01:29:03,140
Sleep this way, dear,

1428
01:29:03,141 --> 01:29:04,340
and stretch out your feet.

1429
01:29:04,341 --> 01:29:06,540
You heard what the doctor said, right?

1430
01:29:06,541 --> 01:29:09,420
Perumayi?
What happened?

1431
01:29:09,421 --> 01:29:12,340
Why are you here
without sending them to school?

1432
01:29:12,341 --> 01:29:14,821
What a sudden surprise, Perumayi!

1433
01:29:15,101 --> 01:29:16,701
What brings you here?

1434
01:29:17,221 --> 01:29:20,020
- You'll have some koozh?
- Garnish it with some poison for me.

1435
01:29:20,021 --> 01:29:21,461
I'd rather die than stay alive!

1436
01:29:22,701 --> 01:29:24,660
What's wrong with her?

1437
01:29:24,661 --> 01:29:26,341
What happened, dear?

1438
01:29:26,661 --> 01:29:28,061
Mom will tell you, Granny.

1439
01:29:28,301 --> 01:29:29,541
Where's Brother?

1440
01:29:41,341 --> 01:29:43,420
- Hello, Baskar!
- Hi!

1441
01:29:43,421 --> 01:29:45,260
You two keep talking.
We'll join you in a while.

1442
01:29:45,261 --> 01:29:46,141
Okay.

1443
01:29:52,461 --> 01:29:55,221
She took such good care of us,

1444
01:29:55,501 --> 01:29:57,581
wouldn't she know
what's best for her own life?

1445
01:29:58,301 --> 01:29:59,341
Which is why,

1446
01:30:00,741 --> 01:30:03,861
whatever Mom likes,
we’ll support it too!

1447
01:30:07,301 --> 01:30:08,461
I scared you good, huh?

1448
01:30:10,381 --> 01:30:12,221
Nah, nah.
Must've been the others.

1449
01:30:12,821 --> 01:30:16,341
I knew you'd have your reasons
since you're a well educated boy.

1450
01:30:16,861 --> 01:30:18,021
Um…

1451
01:30:19,421 --> 01:30:20,421
Can I…

1452
01:30:21,101 --> 01:30:22,341
Can I know what that was?

1453
01:30:24,301 --> 01:30:27,501
Before I got here,
I first visited my Aunt.

1454
01:30:27,661 --> 01:30:29,141
Baskar, here you go.

1455
01:30:29,381 --> 01:30:31,381
- What's the matter?
- You know how…

1456
01:30:32,541 --> 01:30:33,701
Mom… for a long time…

1457
01:30:34,581 --> 01:30:35,661
She's been alone for a long time.

1458
01:30:36,461 --> 01:30:38,981
So… I thought…

1459
01:30:39,941 --> 01:30:41,900
Get up, you scoundrel!

1460
01:30:41,901 --> 01:30:43,901
And get out of my house!

1461
01:30:44,781 --> 01:30:48,901
Do the same for your aunt
and her children! I dare you!

1462
01:30:57,901 --> 01:30:59,981
Now every relative will line up

1463
01:31:00,381 --> 01:31:02,821
to try and shatter Mom's strength.

1464
01:31:03,021 --> 01:31:03,981
Another thing.

1465
01:31:04,381 --> 01:31:07,101
Since I didn't want everyone to know
when the wedding is,

1466
01:31:07,661 --> 01:31:09,941
I couldn't give my approval
in the morning.

1467
01:31:10,341 --> 01:31:11,540
Sorry.

1468
01:31:11,541 --> 01:31:12,541
So…

1469
01:31:12,861 --> 01:31:14,061
We're getting married in secret?

1470
01:31:14,181 --> 01:31:16,380
That… is impossible

1471
01:31:16,381 --> 01:31:18,741
because my aunt
must've told her parents by now.

1472
01:31:19,221 --> 01:31:21,501
And it won't take long
for the news to spread from there.

1473
01:31:22,861 --> 01:31:25,101
The only information they'll receive
is of your marriage.

1474
01:31:25,501 --> 01:31:27,381
But when it is happening

1475
01:31:27,501 --> 01:31:28,861
is something they'll never, ever know.

1476
01:31:28,981 --> 01:31:30,781
Make sure of it, okay?

1477
01:31:32,101 --> 01:31:34,301
Can I know when I'm getting married?

1478
01:31:34,621 --> 01:31:35,741
When's the wedding?

1479
01:31:36,661 --> 01:31:37,661
Tell me.

1480
01:31:39,021 --> 01:31:40,061
See that?

1481
01:31:41,341 --> 01:31:44,541
It's when the sun sets
and rises again.

1482
01:31:45,781 --> 01:31:48,661
You mean, in the morning?
Tomorrow?!

1483
01:31:49,061 --> 01:31:50,221
This is a wedding!

1484
01:31:50,341 --> 01:31:52,741
- We've to get the thaali, decor--
- We must make haste.

1485
01:31:53,741 --> 01:31:55,420
I haven't conveyed this
to my mom yet.

1486
01:31:55,421 --> 01:31:57,300
I just decided this.

1487
01:31:57,301 --> 01:31:58,661
I'll take care of it all.

1488
01:31:59,581 --> 01:32:02,021
I'll let you know
in which temple it will be in.

1489
01:32:02,741 --> 01:32:05,101
- See you! He'll convey everything!
- [both] Sure, dear. See you!

1490
01:32:27,181 --> 01:32:28,061
Dad?

1491
01:32:40,501 --> 01:32:41,701
Yes, dear.

1492
01:32:42,941 --> 01:32:45,741
You can call those
near and dear to you.

1493
01:32:46,181 --> 01:32:49,901
I noticed I made my sister
upset in the morning.

1494
01:32:51,741 --> 01:32:53,061
So, I'd like to…

1495
01:32:53,301 --> 01:32:54,501
Sembaruthi's her name, right?

1496
01:32:54,701 --> 01:32:56,181
Yeah.

1497
01:32:56,621 --> 01:32:59,301
I'll invite Sembaruthi myself.

1498
01:33:02,461 --> 01:33:03,381
Baskar?

1499
01:33:05,061 --> 01:33:06,941
You’ve been my saving grace.

1500
01:33:10,181 --> 01:33:11,301
Actually…

1501
01:33:12,661 --> 01:33:14,581
Mom just met you

1502
01:33:15,621 --> 01:33:16,941
and I just met you.

1503
01:33:18,541 --> 01:33:20,261
We have no idea who you are

1504
01:33:21,341 --> 01:33:23,421
and trust you blindly
to marry our mother.

1505
01:33:24,101 --> 01:33:24,981
I ask you…

1506
01:33:25,381 --> 01:33:27,381
to please be
my mother's saving grace!

1507
01:33:31,101 --> 01:33:32,221
Alright, dear!

1508
01:33:33,541 --> 01:33:34,781
Alright!

1509
01:33:36,421 --> 01:33:37,501
Of course!

1510
01:33:50,821 --> 01:33:51,821
Lord Muruga!

1511
01:34:00,341 --> 01:34:03,501
- What’s happening here?
- How would I know?

1512
01:34:04,701 --> 01:34:05,980
- Priest…
- Muruga!

1513
01:34:05,981 --> 01:34:08,661
He never comes to the temple.
Why's he here today?

1514
01:34:09,901 --> 01:34:13,381
He handed me 500 rupees
and asked for a marriage setup.

1515
01:34:13,941 --> 01:34:15,901
He’s not saying anything about
the bride or groom.

1516
01:34:16,221 --> 01:34:19,101
He hasn’t mentioned
the muhurtham time either.

1517
01:34:19,501 --> 01:34:20,861
He’ll come just
ten minutes before

1518
01:34:21,181 --> 01:34:23,101
and wants the temple to be opened.

1519
01:34:24,381 --> 01:34:26,101
Who is getting married here?

1520
01:34:28,661 --> 01:34:30,261
Who told you this, Dad?
Let’s discuss it.

1521
01:34:35,141 --> 01:34:36,060
Excuse me!

1522
01:34:36,061 --> 01:34:38,581
Did Vivek’s brother tell you
that we're getting married?

1523
01:34:39,581 --> 01:34:42,060
Why isn’t he revealing
the bride and groom?

1524
01:34:42,061 --> 01:34:43,301
Go ask him.

1525
01:34:43,421 --> 01:34:45,661
Maybe his friends are getting married.

1526
01:34:45,901 --> 01:34:47,381
Why can’t it be Bhaskar?

1527
01:34:48,781 --> 01:34:50,181
What is this nonsense?

1528
01:34:51,181 --> 01:34:52,860
Dad, I have a lot to study.

1529
01:34:52,861 --> 01:34:53,821
I’m going to my room.

1530
01:34:53,941 --> 01:34:55,981
If you don’t trust me,
lock me from outside.

1531
01:34:57,781 --> 01:35:00,261
- Vivek, are you at the hostel?
- What’s going on?

1532
01:35:03,741 --> 01:35:07,901
Why pension till death?
Shouldn't I remarry?

1533
01:35:19,341 --> 01:35:22,621
We did search for a groom
for Selvi’s remarriage.

1534
01:35:23,141 --> 01:35:26,060
But I don’t know who this groom is.

1535
01:35:26,061 --> 01:35:27,021
Hold this, it’s ringing.

1536
01:35:29,221 --> 01:35:30,780
- Who is this?
- Bhaskar…

1537
01:35:30,781 --> 01:35:34,901
Are you arranging your
mother’s wedding in our temple?

1538
01:35:35,941 --> 01:35:37,261
It's Pachaperumal here.

1539
01:35:37,781 --> 01:35:40,861
Look, you come from a family
that lived well.

1540
01:35:41,341 --> 01:35:44,301
I’m struggling for a life
that shouldn’t be wasted.

1541
01:35:45,181 --> 01:35:46,541
I dare you to stop the wedding.

1542
01:35:50,941 --> 01:35:53,221
Her own sons are arranging her wedding.

1543
01:35:53,341 --> 01:35:54,861
Why should we interfere?

1544
01:35:55,101 --> 01:35:56,140
We must stop it.

1545
01:35:56,141 --> 01:35:59,020
It'll make sense to interfere,
had it been an inter-caste marriage.

1546
01:35:59,021 --> 01:36:00,061
Hey!

1547
01:36:00,221 --> 01:36:02,581
We protect caste
only through women.

1548
01:36:02,701 --> 01:36:05,861
Only by controlling them
can we keep caste order intact.

1549
01:36:07,101 --> 01:36:08,061
Selvi.

1550
01:36:09,101 --> 01:36:10,100
Please come in, brother.

1551
01:36:10,101 --> 01:36:11,981
- Dear…
- What happened to your phone?

1552
01:36:14,701 --> 01:36:15,661
Sit down.

1553
01:36:17,701 --> 01:36:19,181
Have you made tea?

1554
01:36:19,301 --> 01:36:21,781
Hey idiot, did you come here
just to drink tea?

1555
01:36:21,901 --> 01:36:23,221
Hey, sit down!

1556
01:36:23,541 --> 01:36:26,341
Tell me, who among you has
truly kept your wife happy?

1557
01:36:26,541 --> 01:36:28,821
How can they be happy
after marrying us?

1558
01:36:28,981 --> 01:36:30,981
Even after we hit them for small things,

1559
01:36:31,101 --> 01:36:34,260
they stay for the kids
and endure everything.

1560
01:36:34,261 --> 01:36:35,581
- Correct!
- But, now…

1561
01:36:36,221 --> 01:36:39,860
if Selvi, without a husband,
gets married at 43,

1562
01:36:39,861 --> 01:36:42,101
will the women here stay quiet?

1563
01:36:42,501 --> 01:36:45,700
They’ll get the courage to
leave their abusive husbands

1564
01:36:45,701 --> 01:36:47,980
- and marry the right man.
- Makes sense.

1565
01:36:47,981 --> 01:36:49,421
Will caste even matter
to them by then?

1566
01:36:49,621 --> 01:36:52,261
Forget what her sons say.
Doesn't she have sense?

1567
01:36:52,381 --> 01:36:53,781
She’s going to ruin the town’s respect.

1568
01:36:54,061 --> 01:36:55,660
I have three daughters.

1569
01:36:55,661 --> 01:37:00,021
If they know I’m your sister,
no one will marry my daughters.

1570
01:37:00,661 --> 01:37:02,820
My sister-in-laws
already don’t respect me.

1571
01:37:02,821 --> 01:37:06,740
If you do this shameful thing,
I’ll be crying all my life.

1572
01:37:06,741 --> 01:37:08,220
Why were you even born to me?

1573
01:37:08,221 --> 01:37:09,541
We were living in peace.

1574
01:37:09,701 --> 01:37:10,941
Go die somewhere.

1575
01:37:17,141 --> 01:37:18,981
If Selvi gets married,

1576
01:37:19,301 --> 01:37:22,621
the next generation will also
forget our caste pride,

1577
01:37:22,781 --> 01:37:26,100
and will walk the same path
wishing their mothers to be happy.

1578
01:37:26,101 --> 01:37:28,660
Aristotle, if I see you talking to Baskar,

1579
01:37:28,661 --> 01:37:29,701
I'll kick you out.

1580
01:37:30,141 --> 01:37:31,580
We don’t need to be that smart.

1581
01:37:31,581 --> 01:37:32,821
She calls herself a mother?

1582
01:37:36,261 --> 01:37:38,941
You should’ve done this
when your sons were young.

1583
01:37:39,061 --> 01:37:40,500
Why do this rubbish now?

1584
01:37:40,501 --> 01:37:42,060
Is this necessary at this age?

1585
01:37:42,061 --> 01:37:43,341
She’s still not satisfied.

1586
01:37:45,261 --> 01:37:47,700
I came to your house with my kids
and begged you to stay with me.

1587
01:37:47,701 --> 01:37:48,541
Did you come?

1588
01:37:49,141 --> 01:37:50,101
You didn’t!

1589
01:37:50,941 --> 01:37:53,980
You're 66 and you still want
to be with your husband.

1590
01:37:53,981 --> 01:37:55,701
Why? Are you not satisfied?

1591
01:38:09,981 --> 01:38:11,101
Okay, leave it.

1592
01:38:12,101 --> 01:38:13,421
You shouldn't have said that.

1593
01:38:13,861 --> 01:38:15,381
You, too.

1594
01:38:16,901 --> 01:38:17,781
It's her life.

1595
01:38:18,701 --> 01:38:20,261
It should be her choice.

1596
01:38:22,501 --> 01:38:23,301
Selvi, go.

1597
01:38:23,421 --> 01:38:24,621
Make tea for everyone.

1598
01:38:25,901 --> 01:38:27,861
Get up.
Just go.

1599
01:38:37,461 --> 01:38:39,060
Just finish her off.

1600
01:38:39,061 --> 01:38:40,620
This is what she deserves.

1601
01:38:40,621 --> 01:38:41,261
- Close the door.
- Move!

1602
01:38:41,381 --> 01:38:42,901
Marriage?
My foot!

1603
01:38:44,141 --> 01:38:44,941
Don't let go!

1604
01:38:45,101 --> 01:38:48,541
We're supposed to pay the price
for your decisions?

1605
01:38:51,701 --> 01:38:52,741
Don't let go!

1606
01:38:59,861 --> 01:39:01,501
Brother, please spare her!

1607
01:39:01,621 --> 01:39:04,180
How dare you
talk to your mother like that?

1608
01:39:04,181 --> 01:39:05,221
Kill her!

1609
01:39:05,621 --> 01:39:07,941
- Finish her!
- Brother, please let go!

1610
01:39:08,141 --> 01:39:10,500
Mom, please!
Tell him to back off!

1611
01:39:10,501 --> 01:39:12,540
You’ll get married
and leave me ruined?

1612
01:39:12,541 --> 01:39:14,900
Don't spare her!
You witch!

1613
01:39:14,901 --> 01:39:16,661
What the hell, Mom!
Leave her.

1614
01:39:18,101 --> 01:39:20,861
Choke her to death!
Go on!

1615
01:39:22,261 --> 01:39:24,741
- Mom, please listen to me.
- You swine, rot in hell!

1616
01:39:25,181 --> 01:39:27,700
- Hey, back off!
- Mom, please!

1617
01:39:27,701 --> 01:39:29,580
Shut up.
She deserves it!

1618
01:39:29,581 --> 01:39:33,741
Brother, she'll die, please.
Please, brother!

1619
01:39:34,261 --> 01:39:36,621
She’ll go away,
just let her go!

1620
01:39:40,781 --> 01:39:42,621
Brother, come.

1621
01:39:56,021 --> 01:39:58,421
We have to know
who's marrying Selvi.

1622
01:39:59,421 --> 01:40:00,741
But before that,

1623
01:40:00,861 --> 01:40:02,541
we need to know the date.

1624
01:40:03,941 --> 01:40:05,821
Sister Selvi…

1625
01:40:06,381 --> 01:40:08,421
She's dead.
Go check.

1626
01:40:12,501 --> 01:40:14,821
Oh God!
Sister! Sister!

1627
01:40:15,341 --> 01:40:16,301
What happened, sister?

1628
01:40:16,501 --> 01:40:17,381
Sister!

1629
01:40:18,861 --> 01:40:19,981
Wake up, sister!

1630
01:40:20,541 --> 01:40:21,381
Sister!

1631
01:40:21,981 --> 01:40:23,661
Careful, sister.

1632
01:40:23,941 --> 01:40:25,261
Slowly.

1633
01:40:25,541 --> 01:40:26,941
What did they do to you?

1634
01:40:27,781 --> 01:40:29,101
Drink some.
Drink.

1635
01:40:31,901 --> 01:40:33,141
Easy, sister.

1636
01:40:33,461 --> 01:40:34,781
Thank God…

1637
01:40:35,181 --> 01:40:36,141
you came.

1638
01:40:39,461 --> 01:40:40,501
Sister…

1639
01:40:41,301 --> 01:40:47,661
I’m taking the baby and catching
the first bus tomorrow to his town.

1640
01:40:48,821 --> 01:40:51,381
Sister, don't take me wrong.

1641
01:40:52,821 --> 01:40:55,301
The rumour is…

1642
01:40:56,141 --> 01:40:57,141
Sister…

1643
01:40:57,661 --> 01:41:00,981
People like us…
once we become mothers,

1644
01:41:03,181 --> 01:41:08,101
we’re meant to stay
this way forever, aren’t we?

1645
01:41:10,021 --> 01:41:12,301
If we wish to remarry…

1646
01:41:12,621 --> 01:41:13,661
what’s the point, sister?

1647
01:41:16,181 --> 01:41:17,660
If Megala’s life has to move forward,

1648
01:41:17,661 --> 01:41:20,261
if women separated
from their husbands deserve change,

1649
01:41:20,461 --> 01:41:21,861
you take the first step.

1650
01:41:25,541 --> 01:41:26,821
See you, Sister.

1651
01:41:27,621 --> 01:41:28,781
Be brave.

1652
01:41:31,981 --> 01:41:33,181
Take care.

1653
01:41:37,261 --> 01:41:38,541
There, there.

1654
01:41:40,021 --> 01:41:41,861
Alright, sweetie.

1655
01:41:43,581 --> 01:41:45,101
There, there.

1656
01:41:45,381 --> 01:41:46,301
Alright, sweetie.

1657
01:41:50,581 --> 01:41:52,381
We have to stop this.

1658
01:41:52,581 --> 01:41:54,060
Let's smash her house down!

1659
01:41:54,061 --> 01:41:56,460
We’d rather lose a life
than let this wedding happen!

1660
01:41:56,461 --> 01:41:57,581
What day it is?

1661
01:41:58,101 --> 01:42:00,741
Only one person has bought
a nuptial thread from us.

1662
01:42:01,381 --> 01:42:02,461
Even I thought

1663
01:42:02,821 --> 01:42:05,261
people don’t usually buy
nuptial threads on Tuesdays.

1664
01:42:05,861 --> 01:42:07,541
That's right.
Where is he from?

1665
01:42:13,741 --> 01:42:14,861
What is it, Grandma?

1666
01:42:16,661 --> 01:42:17,661
Hey!

1667
01:42:17,941 --> 01:42:20,820
She’s ninety years old!

1668
01:42:20,821 --> 01:42:22,581
She’s lived alone for years now!

1669
01:42:22,821 --> 01:42:25,460
You’re getting your
mother remarried, right?

1670
01:42:25,461 --> 01:42:27,181
Might as well get her married too.

1671
01:42:27,501 --> 01:42:30,101
Someone has to light her pyre.

1672
01:42:31,261 --> 01:42:33,621
Hey! Let go!
Hey!

1673
01:42:40,981 --> 01:42:42,661
Catch him! Go! Go!

1674
01:42:44,261 --> 01:42:45,901
Fast!
Come fast!

1675
01:42:46,701 --> 01:42:48,421
He's going this way!
Come!

1676
01:42:50,581 --> 01:42:51,741
Stop right there!

1677
01:43:00,981 --> 01:43:02,261
You're a disgrace to this town!

1678
01:43:14,541 --> 01:43:16,181
[phone rings]

1679
01:43:17,621 --> 01:43:19,261
[phone rings]

1680
01:43:21,621 --> 01:43:22,541
Yes, Megala.

1681
01:43:22,741 --> 01:43:25,741
- Baskar, I went to your house.
- Yes, tell me.

1682
01:43:27,341 --> 01:43:29,621
Brother?
Hello?

1683
01:43:33,101 --> 01:43:33,981
Hello?

1684
01:43:35,021 --> 01:43:35,901
Hello?

1685
01:43:41,341 --> 01:43:43,701
Manohar, get here as soon as possible.

1686
01:43:49,461 --> 01:43:53,021
Sir, some men beat me up
so the wedding wouldn’t happen.

1687
01:43:53,141 --> 01:43:54,180
Look!

1688
01:43:54,181 --> 01:43:57,701
They tore my shirt off, sir.
This is my friend’s brother’s shirt.

1689
01:43:57,981 --> 01:43:58,981
Okay. And?

1690
01:43:59,461 --> 01:44:01,900
What if they create a scene
at the wedding?

1691
01:44:01,901 --> 01:44:03,261
- Stop.
- Please, sir.

1692
01:44:03,821 --> 01:44:06,941
Around 60 people died in Kallakurichi
after consuming bootleg liquor.

1693
01:44:07,061 --> 01:44:10,341
I got a call from the SP’s office,
so I sent all the men there.

1694
01:44:10,621 --> 01:44:11,541
Do one thing.

1695
01:44:11,861 --> 01:44:14,061
Have your mother’s wedding
in Chennai or Coimbatore.

1696
01:44:14,581 --> 01:44:17,141
- Can't rest a bit!
- Sir. Sir.

1697
01:44:18,581 --> 01:44:22,741
In our village, there are many women
like my mother.

1698
01:44:23,621 --> 01:44:25,741
To bring a change in their hearts,

1699
01:44:26,341 --> 01:44:28,700
I must hold my mother’s wedding
without any trouble,

1700
01:44:28,701 --> 01:44:30,260
- at our temple.
- Hey! Hey!

1701
01:44:30,261 --> 01:44:31,421
Will you shut it?

1702
01:44:31,661 --> 01:44:34,261
The police won’t protect you
just because you want to prove a point.

1703
01:44:34,381 --> 01:44:36,220
Playing rebel, are you?
Get out!

1704
01:44:36,221 --> 01:44:37,860
Why not, sir?
One constable?

1705
01:44:37,861 --> 01:44:38,980
- Just one.
- Hey!

1706
01:44:38,981 --> 01:44:40,940
Who the hell are you
to preach the law here?

1707
01:44:40,941 --> 01:44:42,101
Are you an M.P. or an M.L.A?

1708
01:44:42,221 --> 01:44:44,461
- Why should I protect a nobody like you?
- Why are you hitting me?

1709
01:44:44,661 --> 01:44:47,020
- Get out, I say!
- Sir, please. Sir.

1710
01:44:47,021 --> 01:44:49,581
- Throw them out!
- Go! Leave!

1711
01:44:49,701 --> 01:44:50,821
Give me a break!

1712
01:44:53,661 --> 01:44:54,541
Ezhumalai!

1713
01:44:55,421 --> 01:44:57,261
Valayampatti men are here to see you.

1714
01:44:59,181 --> 01:45:00,061
Come.

1715
01:45:00,181 --> 01:45:01,380
At this hour?

1716
01:45:01,381 --> 01:45:02,421
It's him.

1717
01:45:02,741 --> 01:45:04,541
He doesn't look
like he's here to talk.

1718
01:45:09,061 --> 01:45:10,341
Okay, get here safely.

1719
01:45:10,741 --> 01:45:12,020
Don’t forget the backup battery.

1720
01:45:12,021 --> 01:45:12,901
Okay, bye.

1721
01:45:15,101 --> 01:45:17,661
- Hey! Can't you hide it?
- Let's get moving!

1722
01:45:20,461 --> 01:45:22,261
Hey, you came here
to pay her a visit, right?

1723
01:45:22,581 --> 01:45:25,780
- Why the sudden wedding?
- Hey, things got really messy!

1724
01:45:25,781 --> 01:45:27,021
I had to act fast.

1725
01:45:27,141 --> 01:45:29,380
Even Mom has no idea
the wedding’s tomorrow.

1726
01:45:29,381 --> 01:45:31,581
- What are you saying?
- Megala called you, didn't she?

1727
01:45:33,701 --> 01:45:35,741
Okay, there’s a slight bruise
on Mom’s neck.

1728
01:45:36,621 --> 01:45:38,021
Play dumb.
Like you don’t know.

1729
01:45:39,341 --> 01:45:41,621
Let’s talk about it
tomorrow afternoon.

1730
01:45:45,301 --> 01:45:49,741
Megala would’ve surely told them
about my brother being here.

1731
01:45:49,901 --> 01:45:53,141
Then why hasn’t Baskar
asked about it?

1732
01:45:53,781 --> 01:45:54,941
That wound on his forehead…

1733
01:45:55,261 --> 01:45:56,901
He is keeping mum about it.

1734
01:45:57,661 --> 01:45:59,781
Why has Vivek come here
all of a sudden?

1735
01:46:00,501 --> 01:46:01,741
Dinner is ready, boys!

1736
01:46:40,221 --> 01:46:42,181
Ever since I heard
the wedding is tomorrow,

1737
01:46:43,221 --> 01:46:44,461
I don’t know why,

1738
01:46:45,021 --> 01:46:46,981
but I’m shaking inside.

1739
01:46:49,581 --> 01:46:54,341
My heart feels so heavy,
like a cart full of sugarcane.

1740
01:46:58,901 --> 01:47:00,901
Selvi!
Quick! I'm hungry.

1741
01:47:04,261 --> 01:47:07,181
- I'm hungry, Selvi.
- Come fast, Mom!

1742
01:47:15,261 --> 01:47:17,741
Start eating.
I'll join.

1743
01:47:18,381 --> 01:47:20,101
Why?
All of a sudden?

1744
01:47:20,741 --> 01:47:22,261
Come, let’s eat together.

1745
01:47:23,621 --> 01:47:25,101
He's right

1746
01:47:25,941 --> 01:47:27,261
When the kids were here,

1747
01:47:27,701 --> 01:47:30,101
there was never just one leaf

1748
01:47:30,861 --> 01:47:33,341
or a single plate on the floor.

1749
01:47:42,901 --> 01:47:48,781
I made them all
sit together for dinner.

1750
01:47:50,981 --> 01:47:51,901
But…

1751
01:47:52,581 --> 01:47:53,541
But…

1752
01:47:53,861 --> 01:47:55,421
- From now on…
- Selvi.

1753
01:47:57,461 --> 01:47:58,581
Mom, here.

1754
01:47:59,341 --> 01:48:00,381
Have some.

1755
01:48:14,581 --> 01:48:15,901
Is this the last time

1756
01:48:16,301 --> 01:48:21,661
I’ll have dinner
with my sons like this?

1757
01:48:22,541 --> 01:48:24,701
Sorry, Mom.
I told you a bit late.

1758
01:48:25,821 --> 01:48:27,541
No problem.
Eat!

1759
01:48:27,941 --> 01:48:33,461
Will there be room for me as a mother
in the house I’m marrying into?

1760
01:48:34,261 --> 01:48:39,181
Will they even see me… as a mother?

1761
01:48:40,661 --> 01:48:42,021
Mom, the curry is just…

1762
01:48:43,221 --> 01:48:44,381
perfect!

1763
01:48:46,101 --> 01:48:47,101
Go on, eat.

1764
01:48:48,981 --> 01:48:50,181
- Enough, Mom!
- Mine!

1765
01:48:50,421 --> 01:48:52,581
You!
Here, have some.

1766
01:48:53,541 --> 01:48:54,941
Enough, Mom.

1767
01:48:58,661 --> 01:49:00,301
If they come home,

1768
01:49:01,461 --> 01:49:03,261
they’ll have to cook
for themselves, right?

1769
01:49:05,301 --> 01:49:07,061
- I'll be elsewhere…
- Mom.

1770
01:49:07,421 --> 01:49:08,980
Make the same potato fry tomorrow,

1771
01:49:08,981 --> 01:49:10,261
- but add more oil, okay?
- Hey!

1772
01:49:27,301 --> 01:49:28,381
Mom…

1773
01:49:30,221 --> 01:49:31,261
Mom…

1774
01:49:32,421 --> 01:49:34,181
Mom, why are you crying?

1775
01:49:34,701 --> 01:49:37,141
What's wrong?
Don't cry, Mom.

1776
01:49:37,581 --> 01:49:39,660
- Don't cry, Mom.
- I don't want to go.

1777
01:49:39,661 --> 01:49:42,541
- I'm right here, Mom.
- I'm not going anywhere.

1778
01:49:42,661 --> 01:49:45,381
It's alright.
Don't cry.

1779
01:49:45,541 --> 01:49:48,821
- Don't worry, Mom.
- Stay with me.

1780
01:49:49,421 --> 01:49:50,821
I don't want this.

1781
01:49:51,781 --> 01:49:54,581
I don't want to go.

1782
01:49:55,581 --> 01:49:57,860
Don't cry, Mom.

1783
01:49:57,861 --> 01:50:01,660
It's alright, Mom.
We're right here.

1784
01:50:01,661 --> 01:50:03,221
We're just a call away.

1785
01:50:03,541 --> 01:50:08,461
- Please, don't cry, Mom.
- I don't want to leave you.

1786
01:50:10,861 --> 01:50:12,981
Instead of coming here,
we’ll just come there.

1787
01:50:13,101 --> 01:50:14,021
It's alright.

1788
01:50:14,781 --> 01:50:15,941
Don't cry.

1789
01:50:17,101 --> 01:50:18,021
I don't want to go.

1790
01:50:18,861 --> 01:50:19,901
I don't want to.

1791
01:50:40,021 --> 01:50:41,781
Mom.
It's time.

1792
01:51:48,221 --> 01:51:50,341
- Hello?
- I'm the priest's wife, sir.

1793
01:51:50,501 --> 01:51:53,461
They thrashed him and broke his head
to stop the wedding.

1794
01:51:53,661 --> 01:51:55,341
We've admitted him in the hospital.

1795
01:51:58,061 --> 01:51:59,261
What happened?

1796
01:52:06,701 --> 01:52:08,621
[busy tone]

1797
01:53:27,461 --> 01:53:29,301
Everybody, keep quiet.
Let Pachaperumal speak.

1798
01:53:29,621 --> 01:53:31,260
Whatever happens,
we're with Pacha.

1799
01:53:31,261 --> 01:53:35,141
Hey, we advised you so much
yesterday, and you’re still here?

1800
01:53:36,781 --> 01:53:40,300
If you really want this widow's hands,
do it in your town's temple.

1801
01:53:40,301 --> 01:53:41,140
Yes. Get out of here.

1802
01:53:41,141 --> 01:53:42,061
Who's the widow here?

1803
01:53:43,141 --> 01:53:45,941
I was alone for
the past six and a half years.

1804
01:53:46,581 --> 01:53:48,301
Now, she's here
to be my companion.

1805
01:53:48,661 --> 01:53:49,661
Not only that.

1806
01:53:50,461 --> 01:53:53,461
To be honest, she's the one
saving this wayward.

1807
01:53:55,301 --> 01:53:56,221
What?!

1808
01:53:56,381 --> 01:53:58,461
A woman saving a man?!

1809
01:53:58,741 --> 01:53:59,941
Interesting.

1810
01:54:01,301 --> 01:54:02,621
Come on, Baskar.

1811
01:54:14,861 --> 01:54:15,981
Go, bring it.

1812
01:54:36,821 --> 01:54:37,901
Action.

1813
01:55:01,901 --> 01:55:03,741
Come on. Cover the situation
from all the sides.

1814
01:55:03,861 --> 01:55:04,941
Fast!

1815
01:55:05,541 --> 01:55:07,541
Every dumbo of the village is here.
Cover them.

1816
01:55:07,861 --> 01:55:09,621
Ready, Ready!
Camera 4, be ready.

1817
01:55:09,781 --> 01:55:10,661
Yes, Kimki.

1818
01:55:11,101 --> 01:55:13,021
Drones shouldn't move
without my say.

1819
01:55:13,141 --> 01:55:14,100
Okay, sir.

1820
01:55:14,101 --> 01:55:15,580
- Sandhya, go live.
- Done!

1821
01:55:15,581 --> 01:55:17,300
Who are these people?
Why are so many of them here?

1822
01:55:17,301 --> 01:55:18,780
Our channel's bringing
a sensational content.

1823
01:55:18,781 --> 01:55:20,540
Brilliant idea! Amazing, Baskar!

1824
01:55:20,541 --> 01:55:21,461
Sir, your name?

1825
01:55:21,661 --> 01:55:22,820
He's Pacha.
Pachaperumal.

1826
01:55:22,821 --> 01:55:24,020
Oh, it's him?

1827
01:55:24,021 --> 01:55:25,660
The right to remarry,
regardless of gender,

1828
01:55:25,661 --> 01:55:27,341
was recognized
even during the British period.

1829
01:55:27,501 --> 01:55:29,380
Do you know that it's a crime
to oppose it?

1830
01:55:29,381 --> 01:55:30,660
- What? Crime?!
- He's pushing the mic.

1831
01:55:30,661 --> 01:55:31,500
- A crime?
- Yes.

1832
01:55:31,501 --> 01:55:33,381
You'll be locked up
for two and a half years. Know that?

1833
01:55:33,981 --> 01:55:36,860
Did you hear that, man?
Jail for two and a half years!

1834
01:55:36,861 --> 01:55:37,861
Why meddle in this?

1835
01:55:38,581 --> 01:55:40,421
Drone C, capture that long haired guy.

1836
01:55:40,621 --> 01:55:41,740
Go near him.

1837
01:55:41,741 --> 01:55:43,141
- Go, go!
- Yes, sir. Sure.

1838
01:55:47,261 --> 01:55:48,581
Look! They've even got billhooks!

1839
01:55:48,701 --> 01:55:51,100
- Zoom in!
- Camera 4, focus on the weapons.

1840
01:55:51,101 --> 01:55:52,501
Very good! Very good!

1841
01:55:52,621 --> 01:55:54,740
You're here to stop a remarriage
with weapons.

1842
01:55:54,741 --> 01:55:56,260
- That'll get you seven and a half years.
- What?!

1843
01:55:56,261 --> 01:55:59,901
Seven and a half years?!
Pacha is trying to get us locked up, man.

1844
01:56:00,021 --> 01:56:01,980
This is being telecast live.
Do you know that?

1845
01:56:01,981 --> 01:56:04,301
- What's that?
- Means the entire town is watching us.

1846
01:56:04,421 --> 01:56:06,261
Town?!
The entire world is watching us.

1847
01:56:06,421 --> 01:56:09,420
Our faces would be on
the wanted list now.

1848
01:56:09,421 --> 01:56:11,060
He's in a government job.

1849
01:56:11,061 --> 01:56:12,101
Leave him.

1850
01:56:12,221 --> 01:56:13,300
Run away, man.

1851
01:56:13,301 --> 01:56:15,181
Drone C, follow the hair guy.

1852
01:56:15,301 --> 01:56:16,381
He's moving back.

1853
01:56:16,701 --> 01:56:18,301
He's trying to hide behind the crowd.
Don't let him.

1854
01:56:18,701 --> 01:56:21,381
He'll mess up our plan.
Focus on him.

1855
01:56:21,501 --> 01:56:23,821
Leave my shirt, man.
How will you even hide here?

1856
01:56:24,021 --> 01:56:27,181
- How many liters of liquor did you get?
- Are you trying to get us arrested?

1857
01:56:27,741 --> 01:56:29,541
I've seen this somewhere.

1858
01:56:29,661 --> 01:56:30,900
Me too, man.

1859
01:56:30,901 --> 01:56:34,021
- She's telling that we'll get seven years.
- And this thing keeps following us.

1860
01:56:34,621 --> 01:56:36,900
Now I know what this is.

1861
01:56:36,901 --> 01:56:39,100
It's… 'that', right?

1862
01:56:39,101 --> 01:56:40,901
2020
CORONA TIME

1863
01:56:41,061 --> 01:56:44,220
Oh, god! Please!
Don't take me.

1864
01:56:44,221 --> 01:56:46,541
Where did my mom go?

1865
01:56:46,661 --> 01:56:49,860
That's it! Super!

1866
01:56:49,861 --> 01:56:52,741
Great job! Awesome!

1867
01:56:52,861 --> 01:56:55,220
I still remember the thrashings.

1868
01:56:55,221 --> 01:56:57,701
- You're the carrom board guy, right?
- Yeah, man.

1869
01:56:58,461 --> 01:57:00,741
Oh, God!
The police is watching.

1870
01:57:01,021 --> 01:57:02,141
Run!

1871
01:57:02,261 --> 01:57:05,181
The crowd is scattering.
Put the drones on them.

1872
01:57:05,381 --> 01:57:07,061
Hey, stop. Don't run.

1873
01:57:08,021 --> 01:57:09,301
Why are you running?

1874
01:57:09,861 --> 01:57:12,061
Deal this Pacha.

1875
01:57:12,181 --> 01:57:13,381
Drone A, head toward the river.

1876
01:57:13,701 --> 01:57:14,941
Sandhya,
put Drone B on the live feed.

1877
01:57:16,061 --> 01:57:18,781
That guy doesn't even
care about his dhoti. Catch him.

1878
01:57:20,661 --> 01:57:22,981
Leave no one.
Just follow them.

1879
01:57:27,221 --> 01:57:30,061
Look! That one is showing us his rear.
Cover him.

1880
01:57:30,181 --> 01:57:31,141
Cover his face.

1881
01:57:31,261 --> 01:57:34,421
Look that friend in need
and the friend in deed. Cover them, too.

1882
01:57:35,941 --> 01:57:37,181
Start the vehicle.

1883
01:57:37,341 --> 01:57:38,940
Hold Camera 4 on this spot. Let's go!

1884
01:57:38,941 --> 01:57:41,661
Follow them till they reach
the village border.

1885
01:57:41,901 --> 01:57:43,380
Run, guys!

1886
01:57:43,381 --> 01:57:45,501
Pacha, you're dead.
Don't ever think of coming back.

1887
01:57:46,501 --> 01:57:49,301
Didn't you say that the entire
village will stand beside you?

1888
01:57:49,661 --> 01:57:50,661
I see no one.

1889
01:57:50,821 --> 01:57:51,861
Only he is here.

1890
01:58:03,621 --> 01:58:05,181
Ezhumalai.
Whack him, man.

1891
01:58:07,061 --> 01:58:08,421
Do you know anything about
cutting sugarcane?

1892
01:58:09,661 --> 01:58:10,901
One slash near the root.

1893
01:58:12,221 --> 01:58:13,501
One slash in the middle.

1894
01:58:14,581 --> 01:58:17,461
In the third slash, the leaf sheath
goes to the trash,

1895
01:58:17,741 --> 01:58:18,981
and the cane joins the load.

1896
01:58:29,821 --> 01:58:31,981
Someone has already done our job.

1897
01:58:32,941 --> 01:58:34,701
Hey, arrest him.

1898
01:58:34,941 --> 01:58:37,501
Hey, you've freaked
an entire police station out!

1899
01:58:37,901 --> 01:58:39,821
You could've told me
that you're a media person.

1900
01:58:40,101 --> 01:58:42,501
- What do you want from me?
- I told you yesterday.

1901
01:58:42,741 --> 01:58:44,861
- The wedding.
- That's why I rushed here.

1902
01:58:45,021 --> 01:58:47,101
I'll get them married.
Where is the bride?

1903
01:58:47,261 --> 01:58:48,981
This is your mom, right?

1904
01:58:49,181 --> 01:58:51,701
Why are you holding the garland?
It'll be heavy. Give it to me.

1905
01:58:51,821 --> 01:58:53,941
He's the groom, right?

1906
01:58:54,461 --> 01:58:56,060
It's him. I can tell.

1907
01:58:56,061 --> 01:58:57,781
And, where are the media people?

1908
01:58:57,901 --> 01:58:59,261
They were covering those guys.

1909
01:58:59,421 --> 01:59:00,501
Look!

1910
01:59:01,461 --> 01:59:02,381
Come on.

1911
01:59:04,461 --> 01:59:05,581
Vandhana, come fast.

1912
01:59:06,901 --> 01:59:08,181
Now, another problem?

1913
01:59:11,781 --> 01:59:14,061
Don't you get worried.
Be happy.

1914
01:59:14,541 --> 01:59:17,301
With this uniform,
I'll break the lock as well.

1915
01:59:17,541 --> 01:59:18,860
- Where's the stone?
- The priest is not here.

1916
01:59:18,861 --> 01:59:22,860
We're here, right?
There's no need for a priest.

1917
01:59:22,861 --> 01:59:23,820
Then, action!

1918
01:59:23,821 --> 01:59:24,901
I'll break it now.

1919
01:59:25,061 --> 01:59:25,901
Cut!

1920
01:59:26,061 --> 01:59:27,781
- Who the hell is he?
- Baskar, this is too much.

1921
01:59:28,661 --> 01:59:30,861
The script might be yours.
But, I'm the director.

1922
01:59:31,341 --> 01:59:32,301
ACTION!

1923
01:59:32,981 --> 01:59:34,621
2019
APRIL 17

1924
01:59:36,781 --> 01:59:38,941
KALLAKURICHI
VALAYAMPATTU

1925
01:59:40,861 --> 01:59:43,661
EZHUMALAI AND SELVI IN REAL LIFE

1926
02:00:07,341 --> 02:00:09,780
AFTER A FEW MONTHS
FLEW BY…

1927
02:00:09,781 --> 02:00:11,820
I'm guessing you're here
for something special.

1928
02:00:11,821 --> 02:00:12,940
How can I help?

1929
02:00:12,941 --> 02:00:15,141
I'm here to look for a groom
for my daughter-in-law.

1930
02:00:17,661 --> 02:00:19,861
Hey! She is Megala from my village.

1931
02:00:20,221 --> 02:00:22,020
The marriage will definitely happen.

1932
02:00:22,021 --> 02:00:23,741
Are you happy?

1933
02:00:28,221 --> 02:00:29,900
- Baskar! Vivek!
- Hi, Dad.

1934
02:00:29,901 --> 02:00:31,020
- Hi, Dad.
- Give me your bag.

1935
02:00:31,021 --> 02:00:32,380
- It's fine, Dad.
- Are you guys hungry?

1936
02:00:32,381 --> 02:00:33,341
- Yeah.
- We'll be there soon.

1937
02:00:33,661 --> 02:00:34,621
Get on.

1938
02:00:35,581 --> 02:00:36,821
- Shall we?
- Yes.

1939
02:00:42,741 --> 02:00:44,221
It will be spicy, man.

1940
02:00:45,461 --> 02:00:48,981
Dad, Mom won't eat
until we reach.

1941
02:00:49,101 --> 02:00:50,381
At least you could've eaten.

1942
02:00:50,581 --> 02:00:53,101
But, I didn't marry her
to sit and eat alone.

1943
02:00:53,621 --> 02:00:55,181
It's not a big deal.

1944
02:00:55,821 --> 02:00:58,021
Instead of turning Mom into a stone

1945
02:00:58,181 --> 02:01:00,541
by calling her an idol or a goddess…

1946
02:01:00,741 --> 02:01:04,501
you saw her as a human,
respected her and stood by her.

1947
02:01:04,701 --> 02:01:06,181
That's what matters.

1948
02:01:06,301 --> 02:01:08,021
It was all my brother.

1949
02:01:08,781 --> 02:01:10,021
- Some for you.
- Dad.

1950
02:01:10,381 --> 02:01:11,981
We're mere knives.

1951
02:01:12,301 --> 02:01:15,541
Only she had the courage
to wield it.

1952
02:01:15,901 --> 02:01:18,501
My mom, who believed
life can begin at any age,

1953
02:01:18,621 --> 02:01:21,461
is truly on another level.

1954
02:01:28,261 --> 02:01:29,581
- Give me that.
- Here.

1955
02:01:29,741 --> 02:01:31,301
- Vivek, have more eggs.
- Sure.

1956
02:01:31,501 --> 02:01:32,381
Give one to Baskar.

1957
02:01:33,541 --> 02:01:35,301
Have some more potatoes.

1958
02:01:35,421 --> 02:01:37,061
- Eat well.
- Mom, it's amazing.

1959
02:01:37,261 --> 02:01:38,141
Of course.

1960
02:01:38,941 --> 02:01:40,781
Hey, you have payasam for dessert.

1961
02:01:41,101 --> 02:01:42,781
- Wow!
- Dad made it.

1962
02:01:52,421 --> 02:01:57,181
Subtitles by QUBE

